.com/users/loci-admin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/loci-admin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/loci-admin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/loci-admin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/loci-admin","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kenilam/Ki.CL-arm/commits/b592d0f2296c6029f6ba4ea920e5724d9e127870/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T00:00:43Z","email":"admin@loci.world","name":"Keni Lam"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T00:00:43Z","email":"admin@loci.world","name":"Keni Lam"},"message":"feat: the switch is instant and the floor waits for it\n\nThe wire to the bridge is dialled once and kept, so putting the arms\nback on it costs nothing after the first time; a link off it takes only\nits own ear, and the arms it leaves stay held. While any arm is between\nlinks the whole floor pauses, belts and arms alike, so the switch is one\npause and nothing moves on without the arm working it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9e24f560861a99f8218ab782e0a62a8be80148e8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kenilam/Ki.CL-arm/git/trees/9e24f560861a99f8218ab782e0a62a8be80148e8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kenilam/Ki.CL-arm/git/commits/b592d0f2296c6029f6ba4ea920e5724d9e127870","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/141117197?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/loci-admin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/loci-admin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/loci-admin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/loci-admin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/loci-admin","id":141117197,"login":"loc