.com/users/kenilam","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kenilam/Ki.CL-arm/commits/6f096ec16e31838327516edf567823e9e7f0843f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T17:37:30Z","email":"hello@ki-cl.com","name":"Keni Lam"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T17:37:30Z","email":"hello@ki-cl.com","name":"Keni Lam"},"message":"feat(sim): our arm in Isaac Sim, on ROS 2\n\nsim/arm.urdf is the controller''s arm: the same link lengths, and joints\nnamed and signed as the controller''s own, so a joint target goes to the\nsimulator as computed and a joint state comes back the same way.\nsim/scene.py imports it with acceleration drives and puts each arm on\n/<id>/joint_states and /<id>/joint_commands. `make gcp.sim` ships and starts\nit. Verified: 62 Hz joint states, and a held target reached to within\ngravity sag.\n\nThe Franka in the shipped MoveIt example reaches 0.85 m; the hub plans for\nan arm that reaches 2.3 m, so it had to be ours.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"385ca23d22856d46796d04715a3751e1a378fa27","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kenilam/Ki.CL-arm/git/trees/385ca23d22856d46796d04715a3751e1a378fa27"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kenilam/Ki.CL-arm/git/commits/6f096ec16e31838327516edf567823e9e7f0843f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/657845?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenilam/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenilam/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenilam/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenilam/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kenilam","id":657845,"login":"kenilam","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1Nzg0NQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenilam/orgs","received_events_u