ps://api.github.com/users/kenilam/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenilam","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kenilam/Ki.CL-arm/commits/1d56e62deb57e19a5adc30e0c7167895ada8d518/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T03:15:35Z","email":"hello@ki-cl.com","name":"Keni Lam"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T03:15:35Z","email":"hello@ki-cl.com","name":"Keni Lam"},"message":"fix(gcp): the named server driver with nvidia-smi, and the NGC key from Secret Manager\n\n`ubuntu-drivers install --gpgpu` left the utilities out, so the check for the\ndriver failed after every reboot and the machine reinstalled it in a loop. The\nscript now installs the recommended server driver by name, marks that it did,\nand stops rather than loop if nvidia-smi is still missing.\n\nThe NGC API key lives in Secret Manager; the machine''s own service account\nreads it and logs Docker in to nvcr.io at boot. `make gcp.ngc` stores or\nrotates the key and grants the access.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a885b2539b4c2dd93865dee7205fef98774b413d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kenilam/Ki.CL-arm/git/trees/a885b2539b4c2dd93865dee7205fef98774b413d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kenilam/Ki.CL-arm/git/commits/1d56e62deb57e19a5adc30e0c7167895ada8d518","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/657845?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenilam/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenilam/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenilam/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenilam/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kenilam","id":657845,"login":"kenilam","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1Nzg0NQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.g