ps://api.github.com/users/kenilam/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenilam/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenilam/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenilam/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenilam","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kenilam/Ki.CL-arm/commits/b9dd50ca14c6116bc52b47b427e8befa7462b7a5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T00:36:03Z","email":"hello@ki-cl.com","name":"Keni Lam"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T00:36:03Z","email":"hello@ki-cl.com","name":"Keni Lam"},"message":"feat: the arm''s business logic as the `arm` federated remote, and its dev server\n\nEverything under Ki.CL''s factory-arm `cell/` moves here, plus the floor''s\nplacement rules, and is built with Module Federation as a remote named `arm`,\nserved at /arm/* the way Ki.CL-back serves its GraphQL client at /client.\nKi.CL keeps only the React floor and imports `arm/hub`, `arm/floor` and so on.\n\nThe server serves the built remote and runs the simulated controllers behind\nthe wire at /arm/link, so the floor''s Physical AI switch has something to dial\nbefore the GCP bridge exists.\n\nAn arm keeps running when a hub goes away, so telemetry now carries the last\nplan revision it accepted (it survives a reset), a new hub numbers its plans\nafter it, and a station sends its rest plan only once the arm has said where\nit is. Before this a hub that started against a running arm had every plan\nrefused until its counter caught up.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e45afc9beaf7175a21e6fcac4660d7e7d0c744d8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kenilam/Ki.CL-arm/git/trees/e45afc9beaf7175a21e6fcac4660d7e7d0c744d8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kenilam/Ki.CL-arm/git/commits/b9dd50ca14c6116bc52b47b427e8befa7462b7a5","verification":{"payload":null,"re