,"sha":"6e4c923eb2f1ceafcc9491c607396060d9ec405b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ssamu04/txm-mattermost/commits/6e4c923eb2f1ceafcc9491c607396060d9ec405b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1210556?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/cursor","id":206951365,"login":"cursor[bot]","node_id":"BOT_kgDODFXTxQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ssamu04/txm-mattermost/commits/03e5d9083d2de65f5e0c43287f092fc04f8138a9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T20:47:49Z","email":"206951365+cursor[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"cursor[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T20:47:49Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"[MM-70936] Show a \"Managed by\" indicator on the Applies-to Users card when an attribute is synced via SAML or AD/LDAP (#38800)\n\n* MM-70936: show a Managed by indicator on a synced attribute''s Users row\n\nWhen a Global Attribute is synced from AD/LDAP or SAML, the Applies to >\nUsers card now opens with a \"Managed by\" row naming that source above\n\"Not editable in Mattermost.\", so an admin can see at a glance that the\nvalues are not editable here.\n\nThe control is the same select the Definition block uses to pick an\nattribute''s Type, extracted into a shared AttributeSelect: locked, it\nrenders as a greyed-out single option carrying the same sync glyph as\nthe \"Synced with\" chip. Attributes managed in Mattermost, and the\nChannels and Posts cards, are unchanged.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* MM-70936: close test gaps found reviewing the Managed by coverage\n\nPin the visible row contents as one string so deleting or reordering the\nlabel, the source name or the helper text fails instead of reading as an\nabsent string, assert the row label order across the Users card, compare\nthe SAML glyph against its chip the way the AD/LDAP one already was, and\ncover the shared select''s per-option icons.\n\nDrops AttributeSelect''s menuAriaLabel fallback to the trigger label: only\nan unlocked select renders a menu, and the one such caller names it.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* MM-70936: assert each select option keeps its own icon\n\nRound-2 coverage proved an option had an icon, not that it had the right\none, so rendering the selected glyph for every option went unnoticed.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* MM-70936: trim the Managed by diff\n\nDrop AttributeSelect''s unreachable single-option `options` default and the\ntest that only existed to reach it, move the chevron onto the menu path it\nbelongs to, and cut comments that restated the code they sat above.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* e2e: align Session Attributes type labels with String/Boolean/Enum\n\nThe listing spec still expected IP and Version, which getDisplayType no\nlonger renders. Also reuse an already-open duration menu so Escape-then-\nreopen does not race the MUI submenu.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* e2e: set MM-T622 override flags via config patch\n\nThe Integration Management Save button stays disabled when the radios\nalready match leftover config. Patch only the two override flags, wait\nuntil they are visible to the API, and store a stable hook-level icon.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* MM-70936: omit Managed by when a plugin-owned field has leftover sync attrs\n\nPlugin-owned attributes should not name AD/LDAP or SAML on the Users row\neven if leftover ldap/saml attrs are present on the field.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* e2e: stage dirty-nav via Enable instead of the TTL submenu\n\nThe unsaved-changes guard only needs a dirty page. Staging TTL opened a\nnested MUI submenu that flakes under Playwright; Enable is a single\nclick. TTL presets stay covered by the persist test.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* chore: retrigger CI after unrelated enterprise cluster flake\n\nEnterprise Postgres failed TestSendClusterMessage/uses_SendReliable_with_just_one_byte_more\n(log assertion missed a line that was already emitted). Unrelated to this PR.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* chore: retrigger CI after unrelated enterprise FIPS cache flake\n\nEnterprise FIPS Postgres panicked in TestInvalidateAllPolicyCaches\nduring teardown Publish. Unrelated to this PR.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>","tree":{"sha":"a6956f2900b6d3f58b1cec1ca8219d36412ae7b0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ssamu04/txm-mattermost/git/trees/a6956f2900b6d3f58b1cec1ca8219d36412ae7b0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ssamu04/txm-mattermost/git/commits/03e5d9083d2de65f5e0c43287f092fc04f8138a9","verification":{"payload":"tree a6956f2900b6d3f58b1cec1ca8219d36412ae7b0\nparent 70658e18d4c6234765af050d051fb1a8a7b2e31f\nauthor cursor[bot] <206951365+cursor[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1790628469 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790628469 +0000\n\n[MM-70936] Show a \"Managed by\" indicator on the Applies-to Users card when an attribute is synced via SAML or AD/LDAP (#38800)\n\n* MM-70936: show a Managed by indicator on a synced attribute''s Users row\n\nWhen a Global Attribute is synced from AD/LDAP or SAML, the Applies to >\nUsers card now opens with a \"Managed by\" row naming that source above\n\"Not editable in Mattermost.\", so an admin can see at a glance that the\nvalues are not editable here.\n\nThe control is the same select the Definition block uses to pick an\nattribute''s Type, extracted into a shared AttributeSelect: locked, it\nrenders as a greyed-out single option carrying the same sync glyph as\nthe \"Synced with\" chip. Attributes managed in Mattermost, and the\nChannels and Posts cards, are unchanged.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* MM-70936: close test gaps found reviewing the Managed by coverage\n\nPin the visible row contents as one string so deleting or reordering the\nlabel, the source name or the helper text fails instead of reading as an\nabsent string, assert the row label order across the Users card, compare\nthe SAML glyph against its chip the way the AD/LDAP one already was, and\ncover the shared select''s per-option icons.\n\nDrops AttributeSelect''s menuAriaLabel fallback to the trigger label: only\nan unlocked select renders a menu, and the one such caller names it.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* MM-70936: assert each select option keeps its own icon\n\nRound-2 coverage proved an option had an icon, not that it had the right\none, so rendering the selected glyph for every option went unnoticed.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* MM-70936: trim the Managed by diff\n\nDrop AttributeSelect''s unreachable single-option `options` default and the\ntest that only existed to reach it, move the chevron onto the menu path it\nbelongs to, and cut comments that restated the code they sat above.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* e2e: align Session Attributes type labels with String/Boolean/Enum\n\nThe listing spec still expected IP and Version, which getDisplayType no\nlonger renders. Also reuse an already-open duration menu so Escape-then-\nreopen does not race the MUI submenu.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* e2e: set MM-T622 override flags via config patch\n\nThe Integration Management Save button stays disabled when the radios\nalready match leftover config. Patch only the two override flags, wait\nuntil they are visible to the API, and store a stable hook-level icon.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* MM-70936: omit Managed by when a plugin-owned field has leftover sync attrs\n\nPlugin-owned attributes should not name AD/LDAP or SAML on the Users row\neven if leftover ldap/saml attrs are present on the field.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* e2e: stage dirty-nav via Enable instead of the TTL submenu\n\nThe unsaved-changes guard only needs a dirty page. Staging TTL opened a\nnested MUI submenu that flakes under Playwright; Enable is a single\nclick. TTL presets stay covered by the persist test.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* chore: retrigger CI after unrelated enterprise cluster flake\n\nEnterprise Postgres failed TestSendClusterMessage/uses_SendReliable_with_just_one_byte_more\n(log assertion missed a line that was already emitted). Unrelated to this PR.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* chore: retrigger CI after unrelated enterprise FIPS cache flake\n\nEnterprise FIPS Postgres panicked in TestInvalidateAllPolicyCaches\nduring teardown Publish. Unrelated to this PR.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqutJ1CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAPLEQAEY4X4lsqCXxxlzmerRStcdp\nWMYCxN7yN+uKsyxJNpM9kzzvbWFU1PJ8wTTT0+Ft9dtsZiECjxAnPYe0UB9c4anw\n2gEAP0ndXdw04Lfj9fKOQdeORJcll3eouRzXKum9iwo9iOOGryhScZYrdr8Kf/hT\n50hfGoa/cENSKzS6vTHaYQWTMg+GVtjXRoSRmGG0tfox1t2QNTu1dypODovhHRIr\nWRYAPzT0P/q8ZLqg3jLWIdKV7xSP8fxs+VdOSA3Velu1hNULjBW9YiPhZo6npom+\nH1Eus6O91ud1jJK5aukJrG0qPeJcs4tdfe1wISCUAJ9FEnxD55D+ET4oioWPWq4p\n4ZgTWDX0zIiyb80VWrfHO5V8kNPwtgbvDCtdUeZxdFTWf9cpgLkRd5NiRdLPtn3x\no51WV45TajY4bKRxr5anyrz7KzoKI5g4qd+r0UclvZuqQDbuGsg3sU+zLXZG2eAu\nPuWjK5l9uJ3sqk3nZmar8Nc4fd8wRSR5kOI7zw6c5kLtJJwtkcQbqf+JA9XPm+m6\nC7RmC+mKVgPq/2BjPJidnJBdK612P1VkVnWwWV/cOy8upb77oGQ9tlfsxODjOQ1Y\nqK/k8VS3jr5AEyRhPXL43FUX3tLJCXJwW5k1Z+2KRukpeW0mDs6zvhJxMVKWp+Fb\ncgvYX8QJ/5ZXKo/6UfxP\n=xBJU\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T10:05:50Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"h