":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17114347?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esarafianou/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esarafianou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esarafianou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esarafianou/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/esarafianou","id":17114347,"login":"esarafianou","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MTE0MzQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esarafianou/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esarafianou/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esarafianou/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esarafianou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esarafianou/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/esarafianou","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ssamu04/txm-mattermost/commits/d584e9264579391221db079dd328106a2632b6a8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T14:41:49Z","email":"eva.sarafianou@gmail.com","name":"Eva Sarafianou"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T14:41:49Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs(site): render IME diagram PNG on PRs that touch it (#38782)\n\n* Add docs-ime-render workflow\n\nRegenerates the rendered PNG snapshot of the IME diagram\n(docs/site/static/img/ime/entadv.png) on merges to master when the\nIMEDiagram component, its content modules, or its logo/banner assets\nchange, and commits the result back to master.\n\nThe live docs site renders <IMEDiagram /> at page-view time, so this\nPNG only exists for external use (marketing decks, PR descriptions,\nemails) where a live React component can''t be embedded. Being\ncommitted and shipped by docs-cd means it lives at\nhttps://docs.mattermost.com/img/ime/entadv.png — a stable URL that\nsurvives branch deletion, unlike raw.githubusercontent.com links.\n\nTrigger paths cover everything the render depends on; the auto-commit\nonly touches static/img/ime/entadv.png, which is not in the trigger\npaths, so the workflow cannot self-recurse. Concurrency group\nserializes runs so a rapid sequence of merges collapses to one final\ncommitted PNG. workflow_dispatch allows the first render (and any\nmanual re-render) without needing an eligible source change.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* fix(docs-ime-render): use npm start so prestart fires\n\nnpx docusaurus start bypasses the npm ''prestart'' lifecycle, so the\nsidebars, OpenAPI reference, and plugin docs are never generated.\nDocusaurus then crashes at boot on a missing require in\nsidebars/api.ts and wait-on times out.\n\nSwitch to ''npm start -- --port ... --no-open'' so prestart runs first.\nBump the wait-on timeout to 10 minutes to cover prestart (OpenAPI +\nplugin godocs) plus Rspack''s cold compile.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* docs-ime-render: submodule checkout + first-run PNG detection\n\n- Enable ''submodules: true'' on checkout. prestart runs\n  stage-agents-docs.mjs which needs the docs/vendor/mattermost-plugin-agents\n  submodule; without it, Docusaurus fails to boot. Matches the setup\n  in docs-cd and docs-ci.\n- Fix the commit-if-changed step to detect an untracked PNG (the\n  first-ever render): stage the file first, then diff --staged. The\n  previous ''git diff --quiet'' only saw tracked changes and silently\n  no-op''d on first run.\n- Drop the ''[skip ci]'' commit trailer. GITHUB_TOKEN pushes never\n  trigger workflow runs regardless of the trailer, and the trigger\n  paths already exclude the PNG output so this workflow can''t\n  self-recurse. The trailer was cosmetic and misleading.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* trigger CI\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* chore(docs): refresh rendered IME diagram\n\nAuto-generated by .github/workflows/docs-ime-render.yml.\n\n* render-ime: widen viewport + hide site chrome before screenshot\n\nTwo visible bugs in the CI-produced PNG:\n\n- Viewport 1280x900 minus the docs sidebar left the diagram wrapper\n  below its 900px container-query breakpoint, collapsing the whole\n  component to a 2-column mobile layout. Bump viewport to 1728px so\n  the wrapper lands at its 1240px max-width.\n\n- Playwright element screenshot captures whatever pixels sit inside\n  the element''s bounding box, including position: sticky chrome that\n  overlays it during scroll. When the diagram was tall (2810 CSS px\n  after the mobile collapse), the Docusaurus navbar bled into the\n  middle of the PNG. Inject a small style tag before screenshot that\n  hides the navbar, sidebar, TOC, footer, and pagination-nav.\n\nThe style injection is scoped to this render only (page-level, not\npersisted), and the export URL flag (?imeExport=1) is unchanged.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* chore(docs): refresh rendered IME diagram\n\nAuto-generated by .github/workflows/docs-ime-render.yml.\n\n* docs-ime-render: drop rationale comments from workflow\n\nDesign context now lives in the PR description; the workflow only\nkeeps the top-line ''what this does''.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* docs-ime-render: bump actions to latest majors\n\n- actions/checkout v6.0.2 -> v7.0.1\n- actions/setup-node v6.3.0 -> v7.0.0\n- actions/setup-go v6.3.0 -> v7.0.0\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* docs-ime-render: drop unused perm + scope push token\n\n- Remove pull-requests: read (workflow never calls the PR API)\n- persist-credentials: false on checkout so GITHUB_TOKEN isn''t left in\n  .git/config where npm ci and postinstall scripts from PR-controlled\n  deps could read it\n- Push step sets its own token-scoped remote URL for the single command\n\nAddresses review from @NARSimoes on #38782.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"3b12f398ea2d5e4ba18a92e8d144442c9250d126","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ssamu04/txm-mattermost/git/trees/3b12f398ea2d5e4ba18a92e8d144442c9250d126"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ssamu04/txm-mattermost/git/commits/d584e9264579391221db079dd328106a2632b6a8","verification":{"payload":"tree 3b12f398ea2d5e4ba18a92e8d144442c9250d126\nparent 5b398474642e8c63dd30e71445046fd2e3392b2b\nauthor Eva Sarafianou <eva.sarafianou@gmail.com> 1790347309 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790347309 +0300\n\ndocs(site): render IME diagram PNG on PRs that touch it (#38782)\n\n* Add docs-ime-render workflow\n\nRegenerates the rendered PNG snapshot of the IME diagram\n(docs/site/static/img/ime/entadv.png) on merges to master when the\nIMEDiagram component, its content modules, or its logo/banner assets\nchange, and commits the result back to master.\n\nThe live docs site renders <IMEDiagram /> at page-view time, so this\nPNG only exists for external use (marketing decks, PR descriptions,\nemails) where a live React component can''t be embedded. Being\ncommitted and shipped by docs-cd means it lives at\nhttps://docs.mattermost.com/img/ime/entadv.png — a stable URL that\nsurvives branch deletion, unlike raw.githubusercontent.com links.\n\nTrigger paths cover everything the render depends on; the auto-commit\nonly touches static/img/ime/entadv.png, which is not in the trigger\npaths, so the workflow cannot self-recurse. Concurrency group\nserializes runs so a rapid sequence of merges collapses to one final\ncommitted PNG. workflow_dispatch allows the first render (and any\nmanual re-render) without needing an eligible source change.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* fix(docs-ime-render): use npm start so prestart fires\n\nnpx docusaurus start bypasses the npm ''prestart'' lifecycle, so the\nsidebars, OpenAPI reference, and plugin docs are never generated.\nDocusaurus then crashes at boot on a missing require in\nsidebars/api.ts and wait-on times out.\n\nSwitch to ''npm start -- --port ... --no-open'' so prestart runs first.\nBump the wait-on timeout to 10 minutes to cover prestart (OpenAPI +\nplugin godocs) plus Rspack''s cold compile.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* docs-ime-render: submodule checkout + first-run PNG detection\n\n- Enable ''submodules: true'' on checkout. prestart runs\n  stage-agents-docs.mjs which needs the docs/vendor/mattermost-plugin-agents\n  submodule; without it, Docusaurus fails to boot. Matches the setup\n  in docs-cd and docs-ci.\n- Fix the commit-if-changed step to detect an untracked PNG (the\n  first-ever render): stage the file first, then diff --staged. The\n  previous ''git diff --quiet'' only saw tracked changes and silently\n  no-op''d on first run.\n- Drop the ''[skip ci]'' commit trailer. GITHUB_TOKEN pushes never\n  trigger workflow runs regardless of the trailer, and the trigger\n  paths already exclude the PNG output so this workflow can''t\n  self-recurse. The trailer was cosmetic and misleading.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* trigger CI\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* chore(docs): refresh rendered IME diagram\n\nAuto-generated by .github/workflows/docs-ime-render.yml.\n\n* render-ime: widen viewport + hide site chrome before screenshot\n\nTwo visible bugs in the CI-produced PNG:\n\n- Viewport 1280x900 minus the docs sidebar left the diagram wrapper\n  below its 900px container-query breakpoint, collapsing the whole\n  component to a 2-column mobile layout. Bump viewport to 1728px so\n  the wrapper lands at its 1240px max-width.\n\n- Playwright element screenshot captures whatever pixels sit inside\n  the element''s bounding box, including position: sticky chrome that\n  overlays it during scroll. When the diagram was tall (2810 CSS px\n  after the mobile collapse), the Docusaurus navbar bled into the\n  middle of the PNG. Inject a small style tag before screenshot that\n  hides the navbar, sidebar, TOC, footer, and pagination-nav.\n\nThe style injection is scoped to this render only (page-level, not\npersisted), and the export URL flag (?imeExport=1) is unchanged.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* chore(docs): refresh rendered IME diagram\n\nAuto-generated by .github/workflows/docs-ime-render.yml.\n\n* docs-ime-render: drop rationale comments from workflow\n\nDesign context now lives in the PR description; the workflow only\nkeeps the top-line ''what this does''.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* docs-ime-render: bump actions to latest majors\n\n- actions/checkout v6.0.2 -> v7.0.1\n- actions/setup-node v6.3.0 -> v7.0.0\n- actions/setup-go v6.3.0 -> v7.0.0\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* docs-ime-render: drop unused perm + scope push token\n\n- Remove pull-requests: read (workflow never calls the PR API)\n- persist-credentials: false on checkout so GITHUB_TOKEN isn''t left in\n  .git/config where npm ci and postinstall scripts from PR-controlled\n  deps could read it\n- Push step sets its own token-scoped remote URL for the single command\n\nAddresses review from @NARSimoes on #38782.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtogtCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQTYQAKMe5AYPOMyidJoy0Oj+GWHP\nqkYigsNcx50uEu8kRrSpBWDWMtuHZxn6NDyqZ43S99ziXEjdaWAG9JmXFpkGASYS\n9F9CfYoRPubLvZM/Hlbm9vNV4ei6PSGgXtJGCcyA4R7EGPIMMGygDXP/81NDfdkx\n/KZ4IMbuAJultmVi3qRyiIEYsmbd6zwnc0+W374IZeaNRlQky1cdstq200LvGKqB\nMl0ladbgs0Q9kLAmCfv1kd9HZ7ZsnmV7mx8w4/AGMRqOmjdgyUJyviSJlUfzlfMS\nzIntRObzca22Xbj1j3