avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1210556?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/cursor","id":206951365,"login":"cursor[bot]","node_id":"BOT_kgDODFXTxQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ssamu04/txm-mattermost/commits/53211e45b6e63e99a5cc64d1ce1b344e3b64cc51/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T20:23:42Z","email":"206951365+cursor[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"cursor[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T20:23:42Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"[MM-61861] Hide \"Manage roles\" for guests so \"Promote to member\" is the only promotion path (#38606)\n\n* MM-61861: Hide \"Manage roles\" for guests in the System Console users list\n\nChoosing Manage roles > Member for a guest sent PUT /users/{id}/roles with\n\"system_user\", which rewrites the user record but leaves TeamMembers and\nChannelMembers on their guest scheme rows. The list then labelled the user\n\"Member\" while every membership stayed Guest, so Team Admin assignment failed\nand Channel Admin was unavailable.\n\nGuest promotion is already handled by \"Promote to member\", which calls\nPOST /users/{id}/promote and migrates the user, team and channel rows in one\ntransaction. Hide the Manage roles entry for guests so that is the only path.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* MM-61861: Cover guest role-menu options in SystemUsersListAction tests\n\nAssert that a guest only gets \"Promote to member\" while a member keeps\n\"Manage roles\" and \"Demote to guest\", including the mixed system_guest\nsystem_admin case and a non-system-admin viewer.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* MM-61861: Harden guest role-menu test coverage\n\nAddress the test-quality review: retarget the non-admin-viewer test at a\nmember so it actually guards the isCurrentUserSystemAdmin conjunct, add\nclick-through assertions that the guest path opens the promote confirmation\nand the member path opens the manage roles modal, and cover the deactivated\nguest and unlicensed cases.\n\nUpdate MM-T1391, which asserted that \"Manage roles\" is shown for a guest, and\nfix the sibling \"Demote to Guest\" expectation whose casing never matched the\nrendered label.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* MM-61861: Fix test import order and drop inert license fixtures\n\nRound-2 review follow-up: the DeepPartial import was ordered ahead of\nUserProfile, which fails the webapp eslint check, and the guest-accounts\nlicense state was threaded through six tests that never assert on\n\"Demote to guest\".\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* MM-61861: Tighten comments in the guest role-menu change\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* Address PR feedback: 0 answered, 1 resolved, 0 declined\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>","tree":{"sha":"f555f2f53f39b5c7d18182952fbef3aa284029ff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ssamu04/txm-mattermost/git/trees/f555f2f53f39b5c7d18182952fbef3aa284029ff"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ssamu04/txm-mattermost/git/commits/53211e45b6e63e99a5cc64d1ce1b344e3b64cc51","verification":{"payload":"tree f555f2f53f39b5c7d18182952fbef3aa284029ff\nparent b94495ffc9e21960768853eec8166cdcf1f5786d\nauthor cursor[bot] <206951365+cursor[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1790195022 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790195022 -0400\n\n[MM-61861] Hide \"Manage roles\" for guests so \"Promote to member\" is the only promotion path (#38606)\n\n* MM-61861: Hide \"Manage roles\" for guests in the System Console users list\n\nChoosing Manage roles > Member for a guest sent PUT /users/{id}/roles with\n\"system_user\", which rewrites the user record but leaves TeamMembers and\nChannelMembers on their guest scheme rows. The list then labelled the user\n\"Member\" while every membership stayed Guest, so Team Admin assignment failed\nand Channel Admin was unavailable.\n\nGuest promotion is already handled by \"Promote to member\", which calls\nPOST /users/{id}/promote and migrates the user, team and channel rows in one\ntransaction. Hide the Manage roles entry for guests so that is the only path.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* MM-61861: Cover guest role-menu options in SystemUsersListAction tests\n\nAssert that a guest only gets \"Promote to member\" while a member keeps\n\"Manage roles\" and \"Demote to guest\", including the mixed system_guest\nsystem_admin case and a non-system-admin viewer.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* MM-61861: Harden guest role-menu test coverage\n\nAddress the test-quality review: retarget the non-admin-viewer test at a\nmember so it actually guards the isCurrentUserSystemAdmin conjunct, add\nclick-through assertions that the guest path opens the promote confirmation\nand the member path opens the manage roles modal, and cover the deactivated\nguest and unlicensed cases.\n\nUpdate MM-T1391, which asserted that \"Manage roles\" is shown for a guest, and\nfix the sibling \"Demote to Guest\" expectation whose casing never matched the\nrendered label.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* MM-61861: Fix test import order and drop inert license fixtures\n\nRound-2 review follow-up: the DeepPartial import was ordered ahead of\nUserProfile, which fails the webapp eslint check, and the guest-accounts\nlicense state was threaded through six tests that never assert on\n\"Demote to guest\".\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* MM-61861: Tighten comments in the guest role-menu change\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* Address PR feedback: 0 answered, 1 resolved, 0 declined\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtDVOCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA/EoQABp/XNp2zom6su5lxt2GfwP3\nyBQes59SMPRj5YBRgBeNHGWObXTNocRj7O3JMqMhrbjzfE8uLhseq9CXqBmxMhcC\nPyq6PoI0NxG3g3/BUSV/ELyUVMGuOyk7xJs1Nv6GMQYS6RbmENjzsM86e+gYyX2h\nnsd2PO9pGn6/z7PpbX0ctVSMcEmVHtAvwwvPYAPMZCvblziDMRst/teeR9tS/Vt3\nbnwXcZN2V9C+lBWi15E1qKWBb12mFtomitwEZ2I3krApy9mvSUhzbLkvcf34HtHD\n8FrPtAe5kBDulq7pJrXte1V79CL6I8KgEa4Q2/oIrHfXkGx4lmqHgu9oXr7h+5Ud\nzJg3lTriGfdsx8SeIJXd+CH0T/iTzOPQcBnC+LEJKfdgwK4veIlZ4/xeXXBsiI0v\npw4uZ2+HqfhG08adLM3rfftgk1CBGkKcpo3s60Iyqwr8CSma5lEZeKV4fs+Xc6dh\n8/eyWNtArAAFOvm8WQEq2qUcUDfwAKFYiMogvJczpcEylEpHGzWwyPqYG37Futse\nG2Mo+gowxZ8pMMD15Hxdcj6NZQpIpUR2lulh77b3b5OKiYIZiTVFsAPX4bGU8kBJ\nsKc8l7qwREMigUvM7CD28+kvs01n9SOWcolq8+Bg5FNWDiaVOhNRyLCAp2D1kGpb\nT9lP4nFAHm29FohGyde+\n=10JQ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T10:05:52Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ssamu04/txm-mattermost/commit/53211e45b6e63e99a5cc64d1ce1b344e3b64cc51","node_id":"C_kwDOUyPM59oAKDUzMjExZTQ1YjZlNjNlOTlhNWNjNjRkMWNlMWIzNDRlM2I2NGNjNTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ssamu04/txm-mattermost/commit/b94495ffc9e21960768853eec8166cdcf1f5786d","sha":"b94495ffc9e21960768853eec8166cdcf1f5786d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ssamu04/txm-mattermost/commits/b94495ffc9e21960768853eec8166cdcf1f5786d"}],"sha":"53211e45b6e63e99a5cc64d1ce1b344e3b64cc51","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ssamu04/txm-mattermost/commits/53211e45b6e63e99a5cc64d1ce1b344e3b64cc51"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1210556?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/cursor","id":206951365,"login":"cursor[bot]","node_id":"BOT_kgDODFXTxQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ssamu04/txm-mattermost/commits/b94495ffc9e21960768853eec8166cdcf1f5786d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T20:20:09Z","email":"206951365+cursor[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"cursor[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T20:20:09Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"[MM-59493] Accept all 2xx responses from slash command integrations instead of only 200 OK (#38603)\n\n* MM-59493: Treat all 2xx responses to slash commands as successful\n\nDoCommandRequest only accepted 200 OK, so an integration that answers a\nwebhook with another success status (Tines defaults to 201 Created) made\nMattermost show \"Command with a trigger of ''x'' returned response 201\nCreated.\" to the user even though the remote side processed the request.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* MM-59493: Treat an empty 204 from a slash command as a success\n\nA 204 carries no body by definition, but an integration that still sets\nContent-Type: application/json made the empty body fail JSON parsing and\nsurfaced \"Command with a trigger of ''x'' failed.\" to the user. Short-circuit\nthat status to an empty response, which posts nothing.\n\nAlso addresses test-quality review feedback on the 2xx range change: assert\non the interpolated status rather than the full translated sentence, use\ndeterministic table order, and cover the 204 path end to end.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* MM-59493: Correct test comments after review\n\nGo''s HTTP client never follows a 300 regardless of a Location header, and\nDetailedError is withheld from clients unless developer mode is on.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* MM-59493: Treat an empty 205 from a slash command as a success\n\nHTTP 205 Reset Content is bodyless like 204. After accepting all 2xx,\nan empty 205 with Content-Type: application/json failed JSON parsing.\nShort-circuit 205 to an empty response, matching 204.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* MM-59493: Retrigger Server CI after expired artifacts\n\nThe Sep 21 Server CI re-run reused the Sep 17 build artifacts, which\nhad already passed the 2-day retention window, so upload-artifacts\nfailed with \"Artifact has expired\".\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>","tree":{"sha":"9c34ff8379392e8f8e73ab0e3e52c159b6ac25fd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ssamu04/txm-mattermost/git/trees/9c34ff8379392e8f8e73ab0e3e52c159b6ac25fd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ssamu04/txm-mattermost/git/commits/b94495ffc9e21960768853eec8166cdcf1f5786d","verification":{"payload":"tree 9c34ff8379392e8f8e73ab0e3e52c159b6ac25fd\nparent df20dd76df11a6e8ff7d0b9da010a54fc90a736e\nauthor cursor[bot] <206951365+cursor[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1790194809 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790194809 -0400\n\n[MM-59493] Accept all 2xx responses from slash command integrations instead of only 200 OK (#38603)\n\n* MM-59493: Treat all 2xx responses to slash commands as successful\n\nDoCommandRequest only accepted 200 OK, so an integration that answers a\nwebhook with another success status (Tines defaults to 201 Created) made\nMattermost show \"Command with a trigger of ''x'' returned response 201\nCreated.\" to the user even though the remote side processed the request.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* MM-59493: Treat an empty 204 from a slash command as a success\n\nA 204 carries no body by definition, but an integration that still sets\nContent-Type: application/json made the empty body fail JSON parsing and\nsurfaced \"Command with a trigger of ''x'' failed.\" to the user. Short-circuit\nthat status to an empty response, which posts nothing.\n\nAlso addresses test-quality review feedback on the 2xx range change: assert\non the interpolated status rather than the full translated sentence, use\ndeterministic table order, and cover the 204 path end to end.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* MM-59493: Correct test comments after review\n\nGo''s HTTP client never follows a 300 regardless of a Location header, and\nDetailedError is withheld from clients unless developer mode is on.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* MM-59493: Treat an empty 205 from a slash command as a success\n\nHTTP 205 Reset Content is bodyless like 204. After accepting all 2xx,\nan empty 205 with Content-Type: application/json failed JSON parsing.\nShort-circuit 205 to an empty response, matching 204.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* MM-59493: Retrigger Server CI after expired artifacts\n\nThe Sep 21 Server CI re-run reused the Sep 17 build artifacts, which\nhad already passed the 2-day retention window, so upload-artifacts\nfailed with \"Artifact has expired\".\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtDR6CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAzg4QADqWXxfkyOgV9CtKrY8+ng2l\n+jh6IcoF4/O7OgpJDdQ1biCphloV79vJzuYtdrT2CXx6QE0Dk6Lcq8q2GKc/WnaQ\nDYVvfWzxR8GEBXJ6An5UhRjRQb2GKOdwcxBCQa221QU321SPP1HVfZCJbbZ5oeLG\naQDFXJx2ptSKQSWsbB6mDRoNGm+r0W2UieKzLdTgHCWPT/bfmWs4Iado/NzuasY2\nyc