"https://api.github.com/repos/ssamu04/txm-mattermost/commits/df20dd76df11a6e8ff7d0b9da010a54fc90a736e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1415596?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrckndt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrckndt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrckndt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrckndt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mrckndt","id":1415596,"login":"mrckndt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MTU1OTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrckndt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrckndt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrckndt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrckndt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrckndt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrckndt","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ssamu04/txm-mattermost/commits/8ddcd797c7a5801c04831fbbd9104193d1c6015a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T18:17:45Z","email":"1415596+mrckndt@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Marco"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T18:17:45Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Fix K8s HA upgrade doc FAQ claiming manual DB schema migration (#38678)\n\n* Fix K8s HA upgrade doc FAQ claiming manual DB schema migration\n\nThe FAQ said Mattermost does not migrate the schema automatically in\nKubernetes and required manual steps. Both the Operator''s pre-flight\ndb migrate job and the server binary''s startup migration apply\npending migrations automatically, same as any other deployment.\n\nState only that a failed migration blocks the rollout, not that no\nchanges are applied: morph applies migrations one at a time and does\nnot roll back ones already applied earlier in the same run, and\nindividual migrations can opt out of transaction wrapping.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Address CodeRabbit review: transaction-wrapping caveat, startup migration overclaim\n\nState that an individual migration can opt out of transaction\nwrapping (drivers/postgres/postgres.go:211-219), not just that earlier\nmigrations in a failed run aren''t rolled back.\n\nReplace \"so the schema stays current\" with what actually happens on a\nstartup migration failure: server startup aborts (mlog.Fatal in\nmigrations.go on app migration failure; sqlstore.New returns an error\non schema migration failure, propagated up to a non-zero exit) and\nthe pod never becomes ready, rather than implying the schema is\nguaranteed current regardless.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"25ae3245087374210cc4a042bd40bac6e08d785c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ssamu04/txm-mattermost/git/trees/25ae3245087374210cc4a042bd40bac6e08d785c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ssamu04/txm-mattermost/git/commits/8ddcd797c7a5801c04831fbbd9104193d1c6015a","verification":{"payload":"tree 25ae3245087374210cc4a042bd40bac6e08d785c\nparent 371582e1674541acef3a80afd5e1790ba8bfb664\nauthor Marco <1415596+mrckndt@users.noreply.github.com> 1790187465 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790187465 +0000\n\nFix K8s HA upgrade doc FAQ claiming manual DB schema migration (#38678)\n\n* Fix K8s HA upgrade doc FAQ claiming manual DB schema migration\n\nThe FAQ said Mattermost does not migrate the schema automatically in\nKubernetes and required manual steps. Both the Operator''s pre-flight\ndb migrate job and the server binary''s startup migration apply\npending migrations automatically, same as any other deployment.\n\nState only that a failed migration blocks the rollout, not that no\nchanges are applied: morph applies migrations one at a time and does\nnot roll back ones already applied earlier in the same run, and\nindividual migrations can opt out of transaction wrapping.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Address CodeRabbit review: transaction-wrapping caveat, startup migration overclaim\n\nState that an individual migration can opt out of transaction\nwrapping (drivers/postgres/postgres.go:211-219), not just that earlier\nmigrations in a failed run aren''t rolled back.\n\nReplace \"so the schema stays current\" with what actually happens on a\nstartup migration failure: server startup aborts (mlog.Fatal in\nmigrations.go on app migration failure; sqlstore.New returns an error\non schema migration failure, propagated up to a non-zero exit) and\nthe pod never becomes ready, rather than implying the schema is\nguaranteed current regardless.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtBfJCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAE2IQAE7m3okOjCldC1TMGhGzVawz\nNRQ+5b7sWUmYd3IU2cL4+vColiQS/l6foaJcZjSKZULqqnG71jb8M/5eNdBeiehv\nOYKFugER/HUV3OPnLngmGU8dPWvp6Lq6oxoVr8F0gAA69uhbYWrBTmDYHQgvhAEG\nBFhNNPIevQe8U1pQtWvJrcXFslheCMLd4fsMJOKaqqF2VdHkXsrVjxkqZdXHvaoL\nGmbD0Wr+/REY9ce7e1yfAH1ixgfoPHFVPGSC7ztNWom+yBSDjAzGSoywr5Afdhfd\ny3ociLxddMfbYvkz+k5kMsaotm4MeTUgenOrZ3P71XoIp7rK2EpyP4uI9ppRJa7q\ntKLH9RwHNwNwFSkt6BVjUIoRgy95EfVik4lWDFgqttNc2ZCG3Fn33jT3rZX7fLvF\nUaBeubGCpP5cZM90EeFBIDfsZ/O140MXBi3SQMqu4eWAAEcjX+Uj/ghQaPLaAyKA\nW+dvddgEphSPMye4WhWX16GxoSkQQ/zOjTgScr9vg142uWHrqMXOpBc4PzTe+9dS\nlw3zEEQV14hRr6CevcyEkFSzBsY2iv9L2AX0aD0iWCxy8D/vgq8EDc8QgN/beApo\nTm4+EHzeN1xs044zaodUj3L/GNP6HfzZhcxPi7od+IFEQea4y4nsz9NiqEx1lsA8\nTRJShTYoXY4tKv8V/afy\n=aPOJ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T10:05:52Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users