busercontent.com/u/936315?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marianunez/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marianunez/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marianunez/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marianunez/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/marianunez","id":936315,"login":"marianunez","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkzNjMxNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marianunez/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marianunez/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marianunez/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marianunez/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marianunez/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/marianunez","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ssamu04/txm-mattermost/commits/be1bfe55a3aee7fc114323844e4b29e3b0aab6cb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T16:39:18Z","email":"maria.nunez@mattermost.com","name":"Maria A Nunez"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T16:39:18Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Show selected hierarchical attribute values in the profile popover (#38685)\n\nGraph (hierarchical) custom attributes were editable in Account Settings\nand System Console user detail, but the avatar profile popover skipped\nthe type and never resolved option ids to names. Render them with the\nsame name-resolution path used elsewhere, including a walk when options\nare omitted.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>","tree":{"sha":"6ce41a4cb658437dd760b9e938d8bf41fe539c16","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ssamu04/txm-mattermost/git/trees/6ce41a4cb658437dd760b9e938d8bf41fe539c16"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ssamu04/txm-mattermost/git/commits/be1bfe55a3aee7fc114323844e4b29e3b0aab6cb","verification":{"payload":"tree 6ce41a4cb658437dd760b9e938d8bf41fe539c16\nparent ffce664cf5d21bbaabc9b6ca4553d2be9140a2bf\nauthor Maria A Nunez <maria.nunez@mattermost.com> 1790181558 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790181558 -0400\n\nShow selected hierarchical attribute values in the profile popover (#38685)\n\nGraph (hierarchical) custom attributes were editable in Account Settings\nand System Console user detail, but the avatar profile popover skipped\nthe type and never resolved option ids to names. Render them with the\nsame name-resolution path used elsewhere, including a walk when options\nare omitted.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtAC2CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAsPEQAGObpVJyuSZy/bcD83qn6edy\nDcZePSK3HCkGVMpl0jzd3IfZQ5w9yXRv9zBZy+nDxxxk2vCIvZSIUQeUCda2tds6\npSaCawkiq9JOvC5LT3aBQgcG9Qp+ZcKka5CZTlH7ZD2Eea0KD7pjEPKYQyoqwAvT\nGYhXqwSWSIiBSy5K014pzHJK45Sn3XIzj8DTscbUYJ603wgds9jqWG2Ky0bYDaUB\n55NRn6EHyADlp7uOuTJSH//AqYAkvaewSWPZUUaiRUECevBfiPi6iuZQH8LYXhtt\nkrthmZk7Glp1TNkrzcWE6IfmrmPfOgq4RCwiOcg1cyed8g9Zmewgplgsz0QEDkvf\nl/wT5R7Szz6b8jrXGM6U+vE6GFdftfe2LZ9oAkQ/ppikRK7h2sPSYoaZOJc33S60\n2Os9E5coeaFs5yCLEX+T5RmhQu8xL6P4xgPpp7vM/LtFIvoiSROBiz0j6y+Zz194\nAv1DcNwjYgSMXf11AHQgWlMROoVVzRL6MPN6eIo5Xk1JeD1i6B/jjuic5N2XxwUM\n4IhWOcdAiyZPOOQBuMKIguSRZU4/PtI+fJcXqjY8hdBD8vp2zn+IM2l3RbKbonFc\nbpTwH5WY5QC8OnMCfXMi6rsdO6fHPivL85YbHEo9dkYpxYMT0iRSI4Mxv5XdcwgR\nbSreIly47nhFngwoCGEb\n=9iIS\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T10:05:54Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ssamu04/txm-mattermost/commit/be1bfe55a3aee7fc114323844e4b29e3b0aab6cb","node_id":"C_kwDOUyPM59oAKGJlMWJmZTU1YTNhZWU3ZmMxMTQzMjM4NDRlNGIyOWUzYjBhYWI2Y2I","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ssamu04/txm-mattermost/commit/ffce664cf5d21bbaabc9b6ca4553d2be9140a2bf","sha":"ffce664cf5d21bbaabc9b6ca4553d2be9140a2bf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ssamu04/txm-mattermost/commits/ffce664cf5d21bbaabc9b6ca4553d2be9140a2bf"}],"sha":"be1bfe55a3aee7fc114323844e4b29e3b0aab6cb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ssamu04/txm-mattermost/commits/be1bfe55a3aee7fc114323844e4b29e3b0aab6cb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14333569?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esethna/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esethna/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esethna/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esethna/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/esethna","id":14333569,"login":"esethna","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzMzNTY5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esethna/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esethna/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esethna/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esethna/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esethna/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/esethna","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ssamu04/txm-mattermost/commits/ffce664cf5d21bbaabc9b6ca4553d2be9140a2bf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T16:03:27Z","email":"14333569+esethna@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Eric Sethna"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T16:03:27Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Add workspace organization guide and retire channel naming conventions page (#38598)\n\n* Add workspace organization guide and retire channel naming conventions page\n\nSplits product how-to from organizational guidance. The new admin guide at\nadministration-guide/manage/admin/workspace-organization is the single home for\nteam structure, channel naming conventions, sidebar categories, channel creation\nmodels, and notification load.\n\nThe end-user channel-naming-conventions page is removed. Its product rules move to\ncreate-channels as a channel name rules section plus a how-to for adding emojis to\nchannel names. organize-using-teams keeps only its how-to content and links to the\nnew guide instead of recommending a single team.\n\nLegacy URLs for the removed page redirect to the new guide.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Polish workspace organization docs with visuals and review edits.\n\nAdd screenshots from the draft, refine team/channel guidance and cross-links, and keep the teams how-to page pointing to the new admin guide.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Update docs/main/administration-guide/manage/admin/workspace-organization.mdx\n\nCo-authored-by: coderabbitai[bot] <136622811+coderabbitai[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Update docs/main/administration-guide/manage/admin/workspace-organization.mdx\n\nCo-authored-by: Katie Wiersgalla <39744472+wiersgallak@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Update docs/main/administration-guide/manage/admin/workspace-organization.mdx\n\nCo-authored-by: Katie Wiersgalla <39744472+wiersgallak@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Clarify when a security boundary calls for separate teams.\n\nReplace the developer and security operations example with cases where groups must stay hidden from each other, and align the use-when labels.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Remove the unused single-team workspace screenshot.\n\nThe guide never references it, so it should not ship with the docs change.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\nCo-authored-by: coderabbitai[bot] <136622811+coderabbitai[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Katie Wiersgalla <39744472+wiersgallak@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"3df190a24f945e4fab6c41ad4f0ae81e4832ddb0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ssamu04/txm-mattermost/git/trees/3df190a24f945e4fab6c41ad4f0ae81e4832ddb0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ssamu04/txm-mattermost/git/commits/ffce664cf5d21bbaabc9b6ca4553d2be9140a2bf","verification":{"payload":"tree 3df190a24f945e4fab6c41ad4f0ae81e4832ddb0\nparent 86ee66a92d9187ab7e1144007d72039b9fdc1cf3\nauthor Eric Sethna <14333569+esethna@users.noreply.github.com> 1790179407 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790179407 -0700\n\nAdd workspace organization guide and retire channel naming conventions page (#38598)\n\n* Add workspace organization guide and retire channel naming conventions page\n\nSplits product how-to from organizational guidance. The new admin guide at\nadministration-guide/manage/admin/workspace-organization is the single home for\nteam structure, channel naming conventions, sidebar categories, channel creation\nmodels, and notification load.\n\nThe end-user channel-naming-conventions page is removed. Its product rules move to\ncreate-channels as a channel name rules section plus a how-to for adding emojis to\nchannel names. organize-using-teams keeps only its how-to content and links to the\nnew guide instead of recommending a single team.\n\nLegacy URLs for the removed page redirect to the new guide.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Polish workspace organization docs with visuals and review edits.\n\nAdd screenshots from the draft, refine team/channel guidance and cross-links, and keep the teams how-to page pointing to the new admin guide.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Update docs/main/administration-guide/manage/admin/workspace-organization.mdx\n\nCo-authored-by: coderabbitai[bot] <136622811+coderabbitai[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Update docs/main/administration-guide/manage/admin/workspace-organization.mdx\n\nCo-authored-by: Katie Wiersgalla <39744472+wiersgallak@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Update docs/main/administration-guide/manage/admin/workspace-organization.mdx\n\nCo-authored-by: Katie Wiersgalla <39744472+wiersgallak@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Clarify when a security boundary calls for separate teams.\n\nReplace the developer and security operations example with cases where groups must stay hidden from each other, and align the use-when labels.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Remove the unused single-team workspace screenshot.\n\nThe guide never references it, so it should not ship with the docs change.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\nCo-authored-by: coderabbitai[bot] <136622811+coderabbitai[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Katie Wiersgalla <39744472+wiersgallak@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqs/hPCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAiuUQAGVfy5EtA5pD0WIymtRuZW2J\nomhTJS3cAbPwOZtMds3SAp7zF7RBz0YTfwrPv+igtQjjaD5XEcaflFjqgAzLC2l9\nMrPoiEIkzgkT3bgBPV2warQWE/cIo0QyaiSeCRn149En3zBuZBdYlsmqp3tZXKZI\nbpvClPj+7OLT0eB2py8u8E8Kzb12cgBmhjdPvv+/I1yujLGVpv43svWuAxUDzjNa\nNEuppcjFCJBe31qrY7uMrm156dhKzVidJXj7eM43