ollowers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ssamu04/txm-mattermost/commit/da316ef0acb96f728f20014f2bb4886c06ba28c6","node_id":"C_kwDOUyPM59oAKGRhMzE2ZWYwYWNiOTZmNzI4ZjIwMDE0ZjJiYjQ4ODZjMDZiYTI4YzY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ssamu04/txm-mattermost/commit/bc7bb75ce16544448b1cc498abfe2217ef14bfc2","sha":"bc7bb75ce16544448b1cc498abfe2217ef14bfc2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ssamu04/txm-mattermost/commits/bc7bb75ce16544448b1cc498abfe2217ef14bfc2"}],"sha":"da316ef0acb96f728f20014f2bb4886c06ba28c6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ssamu04/txm-mattermost/commits/da316ef0acb96f728f20014f2bb4886c06ba28c6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1415596?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrckndt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrckndt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrckndt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrckndt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mrckndt","id":1415596,"login":"mrckndt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MTU1OTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrckndt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrckndt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrckndt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrckndt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrckndt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrckndt","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ssamu04/txm-mattermost/commits/bc7bb75ce16544448b1cc498abfe2217ef14bfc2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T09:13:12Z","email":"1415596+mrckndt@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Marco"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T09:13:12Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Fix MySQL 8.4+ authentication docs for PostgreSQL migration and server requirements (#38679)\n\n* Fix MySQL 8.4+ authentication docs for PostgreSQL migration and server requirements\n\ndefault-authentication-plugin was removed in MySQL 8.4; the replacement\nis authentication_policy. Document the 8.4+ path in the pgloader\nmigration troubleshooting section, and cross-link it from the\nmigration-assist tool page''s caching_sha2_password warning.\n\nAlso scope the software/hardware requirements page''s\nmysql_native_password instruction to the pgloader migration path only:\nthe Go MySQL driver supports caching_sha2_password natively, so no\nserver-side config change is needed to run Mattermost itself.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Apply CodeRabbit fix for MySQL 8.4 authentication_policy and restore qmynd alternative\n\nScope the mysql_native_password workaround to MySQL 8.4 only (not 9.0+,\nwhere the plugin is removed), add mysql_native_password=ON under\n[mysqld] with a restart before SET PERSIST/ALTER USER, per CodeRabbit\nreview on the prior commit.\n\nAlso restore the qitab/qmynd custom-image alternative in\npostgres-migration-assist-tool.mdx, which the prior commit had dropped\nin favor of the mysql_native_password switch, leaving a dangling\n\"instead\" with nothing to contrast against.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix caching_sha2_password guidance for MySQL 8.0.4+\n\nMattermost''s MySQL driver requires switching back to mysql_native_password,\nnot \"no configuration change required\" as previously stated; merge that\ncorrection into the migration note instead of a separate paragraph.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Lead with the reliable mysql_native_password fix for pgloader migrations\n\nReorder the caching_sha2_password guidance so the working fix comes\nbefore the qmynd alternative, and drop the redundant MySQL 8.4\nauthentication_policy detail already covered by the linked section.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Apply CodeRabbit fixes: correct pgloader image name, scope auth note to pgloader migrations\n\n- postgres-migration-assist-tool.mdx: mattermost/pgloader:latest doesn''t\n  exist; the actual repo is mattermost/mattermost-pgloader:latest,\n  matching manual-postgres-migration.mdx and Docker Hub. Fixed both\n  occurrences in this file (CodeRabbit flagged one, the other had the\n  same defect).\n- software-hardware-requirements.mdx: the linked \"Unsupported\n  authentication for MySQL\" section is scoped to pgloader''s MySQL\n  8.0-8.4 migration issue and explicitly doesn''t apply to 9.0+, so the\n  prior \"if you want to keep everything as is\" branch pointed a\n  non-migrating reader at migration-specific troubleshooting. Scoped\n  the note to the pgloader migration case it actually covers.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5b46211cae467a68544cbe005abc794966f6902a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ssamu04/txm-mattermost/git/trees/5b46211cae467a68544cbe005abc794966f6902a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ssamu04/txm-mattermost/git/commits/bc7bb75ce16544448b1cc498abfe2217ef14bfc2","verification":{"payload":"tree 5b46211cae467a68544cbe005abc794966f6902a\nparent 6249c96b019ba646a8c2bcb5ea9b35dd83e8de37\nauthor Marco <1415596+mrckndt@users.noreply.github.com> 1790154792 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790154792 +0000\n\nFix MySQL 8.4+ authentication docs for PostgreSQL migration and server requirements (#38679)\n\n* Fix MySQL 8.4+ authentication docs for PostgreSQL migration and server requirements\n\ndefault-authentication-plugin was removed in MySQL 8.4; the replacement\nis authentication_policy. Document the 8.4+ path in the pgloader\nmigration troubleshooting section, and cross-link it from the\nmigration-assist tool page''s caching_sha2_password warning.\n\nAlso scope the software/hardware requirements page''s\nmysql_native_password instruction to the pgloader migration path only:\nthe Go MySQL driver supports caching_sha2_password natively, so no\nserver-side config change is needed to run Mattermost itself.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Apply CodeRabbit fix for MySQL 8.4 authentication_policy and restore qmynd alternative\n\nScope the mysql_native_password workaround to MySQL 8.4 only (not 9.0+,\nwhere the plugin is removed), add mysql_native_password=ON under\n[mysqld] with a restart before SET PERSIST/ALTER USER, per CodeRabbit\nreview on the prior commit.\n\nAlso restore the qitab/qmynd custom-image alternative in\npostgres-migration-assist-tool.mdx, which the prior commit had dropped\nin favor of the mysql_native_password switch, leaving a dangling\n\"instead\" with nothing to contrast against.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix caching_sha2_password guidance for MySQL 8.0.4+\n\nMattermost''s MySQL driver requires switching back to mysql_native_password,\nnot \"no configuration change required\" as previously stated; merge that\ncorrection into the migration note instead of a separate paragraph.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Lead with the reliable mysql_native_password fix for pgloader migrations\n\nReorder the caching_sha2_password guidance so the working fix comes\nbefore the qmynd alternative, and drop the redundant MySQL 8.4\nauthentication_policy detail already covered by the linked section.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Apply CodeRabbit fixes: correct pgloader image name, scope auth note to pgloader migrations\n\n- postgres-migration-assist-tool.mdx: mattermost/pgloader:latest doesn''t\n  exist; the actual repo is mattermost/mattermost-pgloader:latest,\n  matching manual-postgres-migration.mdx and Docker Hub. Fixed both\n  occurrences in this file (CodeRabbit flagged one, the other had the\n  same defect).\n- software-hardware-requirements.mdx: the linked \"Unsupported\n  authentication for MySQL\" section is scoped to pgloader''s MySQL\n  8.0-8.4 migration issue and explicitly doesn''t apply to 9.0+, so the\n  prior \"if you want to keep everything as is\" branch pointed a\n  non-migrating reader at migration-specific troubleshooting. Scoped\n  the note to the pgloader migration case it actually covers.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqs5goCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAADTgQAIDT33JAhowNQ0Ip5c/UAi8c\n/cEXFuC6y0ByRxra+/CdaVuTkf1Rb3TkV9b0yi3mPmfMpKOBjDsv6nfLQAhXDU+Q\nyspMppom1VOQpsncYWNwTNFKZ3iCRBOf87CzrwInxOnhfG9f+VQbxxPK2GTjxFZJ\nEvEDsCuNtEY7c/QZ3jAhZ8tG/mq/pmy3uy/aRY9JOTMDScLyf/X2oRzMfQKBY+p+\n7sFSiwpS1NhNq26Wo4FWR+/vEgoeKBrNQIyAz/I5P1BlGOrzWVgq0V8AGf9d4wiS\nA3KeSn+N0UafEO2x8mvFNERIVeaWQ1ZBwXFraCblBOHywHHHhNBgN2YNdK410lTL\n/6c7xBKG5R1bM+sFMFKjv5+eTy6YZVZBATgF61oHibcLJJTz/zsfshNldN8eB5+3\nTlGoE0Ptgn5hXnCSzKU9TLg9wGdTpeVYqx04KNq9O6WtVX7pp9athN8ccEku5nww\npECHzVC6N4NMuZVH3QurdpMCF3D4+r6AaaOchbJpWTz3QLpIrUZxifPdYbs4gQIG\n30qsN/pN7xnWm94rohVfZazutpwAYEUUfKehfnE/E/30WX/kkXkxw0yrLx