/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/cursor","id":206951365,"login":"cursor[bot]","node_id":"BOT_kgDODFXTxQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ssamu04/txm-mattermost/commits/2b3f2e2026c40eb86e7c7fbfd4b2626888d453f3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T15:41:53Z","email":"206951365+cursor[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"cursor[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T15:41:53Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"[MM-61452] Align invite modal channel autocomplete row spacing and slug with the post composer (#38602)\n\n* MM-61452: Align invite modal channel autocomplete with the composer\n\nThe channel autocomplete in the invite modal rendered the channel slug\nwrapped in parentheses and used a fixed 44px row with uniform 12px\npadding. The post composer''s channel autocomplete renders the slug as\n~channel-name on a 40px min-height row with 8px/24px padding.\n\nMatch the composer''s row metrics and slug treatment in ChannelsInput so\nboth autocomplete surfaces read the same way.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* Address PR feedback: 0 answered, 1 resolved, 0 declined\n\nAlign invite modal channel autocomplete with the post composer:\n- Reduce channel icon size to match the composer''s icon\n- Round the autocomplete menu container corners\n- Drop per-row corner radius so rows are flat like the composer\n\n* Use px instead of rem for channel option row spacing and icon sizing\n\nReplace the rem units introduced for the invite modal channel autocomplete\nwith their px equivalents (2.4rem -> 24px, 4rem -> 40px) to avoid mixing\nunit systems within channels_input.scss, per review feedback.\n\n* Address PR feedback: 0 answered, 2 resolved, 0 declined\n\nUse the --radius-s design token instead of a hardcoded 4px for the\nchannels-input menu and menu-list border-radius.\n\n* Address PR feedback: 0 answered, 1 resolved, 0 declined\n\n* Keep generic ChannelsInput fixtures; only add name for slug coverage\n\nThe Off-Topic/Offsite Planning labels were copied from the ticket repro and are not needed to assert ~channel-name treatment.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Stop stacking empty-state padding so no-matches matches one option row\n\nThe no-channels notice sits inside an option, so its min-height and padding were adding a second row of space.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\nCo-authored-by: Matthew Birtch <2040554+matthewbirtch@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"1217ee43616bd0397b788d537c100162e5072d63","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ssamu04/txm-mattermost/git/trees/1217ee43616bd0397b788d537c100162e5072d63"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ssamu04/txm-mattermost/git/commits/2b3f2e2026c40eb86e7c7fbfd4b2626888d453f3","verification":{"payload":"tree 1217ee43616bd0397b788d537c100162e5072d63\nparent dc8e580fa5c1523376a9a36740c56dc148270e87\nauthor cursor[bot] <206951365+cursor[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1790091713 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790091713 -0400\n\n[MM-61452] Align invite modal channel autocomplete row spacing and slug with the post composer (#38602)\n\n* MM-61452: Align invite modal channel autocomplete with the composer\n\nThe channel autocomplete in the invite modal rendered the channel slug\nwrapped in parentheses and used a fixed 44px row with uniform 12px\npadding. The post composer''s channel autocomplete renders the slug as\n~channel-name on a 40px min-height row with 8px/24px padding.\n\nMatch the composer''s row metrics and slug treatment in ChannelsInput so\nboth autocomplete surfaces read the same way.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* Address PR feedback: 0 answered, 1 resolved, 0 declined\n\nAlign invite modal channel autocomplete with the post composer:\n- Reduce channel icon size to match the composer''s icon\n- Round the autocomplete menu container corners\n- Drop per-row corner radius so rows are flat like the composer\n\n* Use px instead of rem for channel option row spacing and icon sizing\n\nReplace the rem units introduced for the invite modal channel autocomplete\nwith their px equivalents (2.4rem -> 24px, 4rem -> 40px) to avoid mixing\nunit systems within channels_input.scss, per review feedback.\n\n* Address PR feedback: 0 answered, 2 resolved, 0 declined\n\nUse the --radius-s design token instead of a hardcoded 4px for the\nchannels-input menu and menu-list border-radius.\n\n* Address PR feedback: 0 answered, 1 resolved, 0 declined\n\n* Keep generic ChannelsInput fixtures; only add name for slug coverage\n\nThe Off-Topic/Offsite Planning labels were copied from the ticket repro and are not needed to assert ~channel-name treatment.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Stop stacking empty-state padding so no-matches matches one option row\n\nThe no-channels notice sits inside an option, so its min-height and padding were adding a second row of space.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\nCo-authored-by: Matthew Birtch <2040554+matthewbirtch@