ub.com/ssamu04/txm-mattermost/commit/4974f1f7c776fff8b1d4c46a41ffbe27cdbbc7ed","sha":"4974f1f7c776fff8b1d4c46a41ffbe27cdbbc7ed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ssamu04/txm-mattermost/commits/4974f1f7c776fff8b1d4c46a41ffbe27cdbbc7ed"}],"sha":"909cadce5e26397239122222273a660b33a62d5e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ssamu04/txm-mattermost/commits/909cadce5e26397239122222273a660b33a62d5e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16541325?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hanzei/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hanzei/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hanzei/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hanzei/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hanzei","id":16541325,"login":"hanzei","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTQxMzI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hanzei/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hanzei/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hanzei/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hanzei/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hanzei/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hanzei","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ssamu04/txm-mattermost/commits/4974f1f7c776fff8b1d4c46a41ffbe27cdbbc7ed/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T07:16:03Z","email":"ben.schumacher@mattermost.com","name":"Ben Schumacher"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T07:16:03Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"[MM-70759] Health Dashboard engine-types (PR04+PR05): rule + snapshot types (#38583)\n\n* [MM-70759] Add healthcheck engine types and accessors\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Use slices.SortStableFunc instead of disallowed sort.SliceStable\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix golangci-lint findings in healthcheck package\n\nAddress revive error-return (SectionErr now returns (bool, error)),\nmodernize (slices.Contains, new(expr), strings.FieldsSeq), and copyloopvar.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Read node Sections independently of Diagnostics in SectionErr\n\nA node can carry a populated section map with nil Diagnostics; gating on\nDiagnostics made SectionErr/Has under-report, unlike the workspace sibling.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Remove import boundary test\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Remove unused CollectedJobTypes accessor\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Read per-node section errors from NodeDiagnostics.Errors\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add TestBuiltinRulesValid to guard the builtin health rule registry\n\nValidate() only catches bad rules if something calls it; this test\nruns it against Builtin() so a malformed rule fails CI at registration.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Make severity/surface/volatility validity checks exported IsValid methods\n\nReads naturally at the call site and exposes the valid enum set to\nother packages that construct rules or results.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Split healthcheck test files to match source files 1:1\n\nEach _test.go now maps to its source file, matching the existing\nresult_test.go convention: rule_test.go, registry_test.go,\nsnapshot_test.go, accessors_test.go, node_test.go.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Gate node diagnostics values on their support-packet section errors\n\nNodeVersion and SchemaVersion read from the support packet only when the\ngoverning section (server_software, database_identity) collected without\nerror, matching the section gating already used by the config accessors.\nClusterInfo-sourced values are unaffected; they are not covered by\nNodeDiagnostics.Errors.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add unit tests for previously uncovered healthcheck accessors\n\nCovers LicenseFeature nil-guard chain and value paths, PluginEnabled\nenabled/disabled/unknown lookups, Snapshot.Leader, ResolvedSubject,\nRule.IsNodeScoped, and Registry.Get/Len.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Drop unused Deployment.ClusterEnabled field\n\nClusterEnabled had no reader and is derivable from config\n(ClusterSettings.Enable). Deployment now carries only IsCloud, the one\nfact that cannot come from config or license.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","tree":{"sha":"bc480818e3bbf5344ae1f0e74e0dbf6fff532e63","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ssamu04/txm-mattermost/git/trees/bc480818e3bbf5344ae1f0e74e0dbf6fff532e63"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ssamu04/txm-mattermost/git/commits/4974f1f7c776fff8b1d4c46a41ffbe27cdbbc7ed","verification":{"payload":"tree bc480818e3bbf5344ae1f0e74e0dbf6fff532e63\nparent 2ddcee9f9543a89f56744b7b336cef0b12807636\nauthor Ben Schumacher <ben.schumacher@mattermost.com> 1790061363 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790061363 +0200\n\n[MM-70759] Health Dashboard engine-types (PR04+PR05): rule + snapshot types (#38583)\n\n* [MM-70759] Add healthcheck engine types and accessors\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Use slices.SortStableFunc instead of disallowed sort.SliceStable\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix golangci-lint findings in healthcheck package\n\nAddress revive error-return (SectionErr now returns (bool, error)),\nmodernize (slices.Contains, new(expr), strings.FieldsSeq), and copyloopvar.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Read node Sections independently of Diagnostics in SectionErr\n\nA node can carry a populated section map with nil Diagnostics; gating on\nDiagnostics made SectionErr/Has under-report, unlike the workspace sibling.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Remove import boundary test\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Remove unused CollectedJobTypes accessor\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Read per-node section errors from NodeDiagnostics.Errors\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add TestBuiltinRulesValid to guard the builtin health rule registry\n\nValidate() only catches bad rules if something calls it; this test\nruns it against Builtin() so a malformed rule fails CI at registration.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Make severity/surface/volatility validity checks exported IsValid methods\n\nReads naturally at the call site and exposes the valid enum set to\nother packages that construct rules or results.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Split healthcheck test files to match source files 1:1\n\nEach _test.go now maps to its source file, matching the existing\nresult_test.go convention: rule_test.go, registry_test.go,\nsnapshot_test.go, accessors_test.go, node_test.go.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Gate node diagnostics values on their support-packet section errors\n\nNodeVersion and SchemaVersion read from the support packet only when the\ngoverning section (server_software, database_identity) collected without\nerror, matching the section gating already used by the config accessors.\nClusterInfo-sourced values are unaffected; they are not covered by\nNodeDiagnostics.Errors.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add unit tests for previously uncovered healthcheck accessors\n\nCovers LicenseFeature nil-guard chain and value paths, PluginEnabled\nenabled/disabled/unknown lookups, Snapshot.Leader, ResolvedSubject,\nRule.IsNodeScoped, and Registry.Get/Len.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Drop unused Deployment.ClusterEnabled field\n\nClusterEnabled had no reader and is derivable from config\n(ClusterSettings.Enable). Deployment now carries only IsCloud, the one\nfact that cannot come from config or license.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsiszCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAmlcQAGaKKAuYJY+AyN6MWLm8RFqE\nTR2V3k/WHFunu5OxO7rwvtbzWNe8xvv7004z1N3q1yBySM1fCRHHKVg9vXqGc8mQ\nnBrUlGfuZcBbR9Gp1sVbw0pwroCqYMg5H7N3DGesQDnD3k8jp7t4eFoOUDF2cRU3\nybKnOeXNrFYBkUnqQ55kgRmIKqewcExBTJEGCSrfH+3mCzIq9wGbx8NkzKL9IVkG\n7cqRx+J4QBkAJB7byAs8/n08kSdeKd/JmhI/ULfXiV2R3FSa7OCcMnP2z5fLIn6V\nWcJj/QF5vj1LlgtuK1GV/SPGPhaHqDf6Rkur4dct9QHF16yXgefRNWXDoggUqFnq\nvRX1H7dAz5Pjqtv613Yb/AEAccrtB0yZAkWcgtTUaIrZ06L0BIRaLljr0XzTtREj\nfZUbL5P/m9jWkj5VFRwtaNeYRHvuYqA+FB5BnQ3POoUqQNr3ED6YZElal1tVu3W9\nBNG+ZCbFqQUqaYltXdHTXXUkkbrLE/YdjeEJIx+MOR5dxgx/d/5NbWJQYXaePPS1\nHNXHJUOko1DOON0WLYvhqoEUeSMCdXugUUqnoTWVO3F8YZJodqpDwbqLpB27mOhQ\noiptFRs2rZXip6QxQvNuIfTIzYdu/mkeMJn8kXLadYew3vGk3GYint0yGP6FwUom\n+wVm1zp1bwYFITnDIFLX\n=FDkv\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T10:05:52Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://gith