jMDNkZjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ssamu04/txm-mattermost/commit/bef024abbe1c2f5c322ec7da869fe3e1355df50f","sha":"bef024abbe1c2f5c322ec7da869fe3e1355df50f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ssamu04/txm-mattermost/commits/bef024abbe1c2f5c322ec7da869fe3e1355df50f"}],"sha":"2ba31db3191b2ab3bf4f04f31e601f77d8c03df1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ssamu04/txm-mattermost/commits/2ba31db3191b2ab3bf4f04f31e601f77d8c03df1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1210556?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/cursor","id":206951365,"login":"cursor[bot]","node_id":"BOT_kgDODFXTxQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ssamu04/txm-mattermost/commits/bef024abbe1c2f5c322ec7da869fe3e1355df50f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T17:02:16Z","email":"206951365+cursor[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"cursor[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T17:02:16Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"[MM-70519] Prioritize the DM with the matched person in the quick switcher (#38224)\n\n* [MM-70519] Prioritize DMs over GMs in the quick switcher\n\nThe \"Find Channels\" quick switcher merged its local results with the\nresults fetched from the server by appending the remote ones, so a\nperson the current user has never messaged directly was ranked below\nevery locally matched group message no matter how well the search term\nmatched their username. Rank the merged list as a whole instead, and\nderive the terms from the sorted items so they stay in lockstep.\n\nThe search prefix used for the \"starts with the search term\" ranking was\nalso compared verbatim against lower cased display names and usernames,\nso typing a capitalized name or a leading @ silently lost that ranking\nand fell back to recency, which favours chatty group messages.\n\nSorting the merged list means group messages hidden from the sidebar are\nno longer implicitly last, so demote them explicitly among otherwise\nequally relevant results.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* [MM-70519] Rank a DM above group messages containing the same person\n\nA group message matches a searched username only because one of its\nmembers is named that, and its display name is the member list in\nalphabetical order, so it looks like a prefix match whenever that member\nsorts first. Rank the direct message with the person ahead of those\ngroup messages, and cover the reported orderings with tests.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* [MM-70519] Derive group message names from member profiles in tests\n\nThe ranking fixtures set GM display names by hand while leaving\nprofilesInChannel empty, so the member names a GM is really matched on\nwere missing and two of the new assertions held without the fix. Build\nthe GMs from real member profiles the way the store does, and assert\nthat the merged items and terms stay in the same order.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* [MM-70519] Tighten the comments added to the quick switcher provider\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* [MM-70519] Retarget the Cypress quick switcher GM assertions\n\nTwo Cypress specs asserted that a group message was the SELECTED (top)\nresult when typing a member''s name, which is the ordering this ticket\nreports as a bug. Both tests are really about the group message being\nfindable that way - MM-T1226 by a name that is not displayed, MM-T3447_4\nby contrast with a closed group message - so assert that the group\nmessage is offered in the suggestion list rather than that it outranks\nthe person.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* Remove temporary test-review probe files committed by mistake\n\nThese two files were scratch jest probes used while reviewing the\nMM-70519 ranking tests and were never meant to land on the branch.\n\n* [MM-70519] Rank quick switcher results on one scale\n\nDemoting a GM only when compared against a DM left quickSwitchSorter\nwithout a consistent ordering: with a DM, a GM and an ordinary channel\nof intermediate recency all matching the same term, comparing any two of\nthem disagreed with comparing them through the third, so the result\ndepended on the order the local and server results happened to be\nconcatenated in. Two of the six input orders put the DM last, which is\nthe symptom this ticket is about.\n\nGive every result a rank on the same scale instead, and reach for\nrecency only when two results rank equally. A group message no longer\ncounts as starting with the search term at all, which is what actually\nmakes it weaker than the DM with the person: its display name is only\nits members listed alphabetically, so it starts with a searched username\npurely when that member sorts first. Ranking also removes an asymmetry\nin the old chain, where two open channels the user had never visited\ncompared as unequal in both directions.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* [MM-70519] Stop MM-T1243 assuming Town Square is adjacent to Off-Topic\n\nTyping \"T\" in the quick switcher now ranks prefix-matching users with\nthe channels instead of appending them, so one down-arrow no longer\nlands on Off-Topic. Drive the spec with two uniquely prefixed public\nchannels so it still covers click-out, arrow keys, and Enter.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* Address PR feedback: 0 answered, 2 resolved, 0 declined\n\n- Replace real people''s names in switch_channel_provider tests with fictional names\n- Extract named constants for the quick switcher ranking demotion weights\n\n* [MM-70519] Lock the quick switcher selection once the user engages\n\nGive suggestion_box a selection lock that is set only when the user\nexplicitly picks a row (arrow keys or hover). Until then the selection\ntracks the top result so incoming results are free to re-rank; once set,\nthe picked row stays selected as results merge in so it can''t be\nreordered out from under the user mid-selection. Typing releases the\nlock again.\n\n* [MM-70519] Rank quick switcher results by recency then conversation type\n\nFold an activity-recency band and a conversation-type order into the\nquick switcher ranking. Results opened within the last 30 days rank\nabove staler ones, which rank above never-opened conversations; within a\nband a DM outranks a GM, which outranks a channel. An exact but\nlong-abandoned DM now falls below recent GMs, a recently used DM stays\nabove them, and a never-messaged person sorts below any conversation the\nuser has actually opened.\n\n* [MM-70519] Rank prefix matches above mid-string matches in the quick switcher\n\nA channel directly named for the search term was ranking below direct\nmessages that only contained the term somewhere in the middle. Add a\nprefix-match tier to searchRank, below recency but above conversation\ntype, so a prefix-matching result (e.g. the Off-Topic channel) is not\nburied under DMs that merely mention the term.\n\n* Log quick switcher ranking breakdown in developer mode\n\nAdds a developer-mode-only console.table that prints, for each provided\nresult list, the per-result rank and the penalty breakdown (activity,\nprefix vs mid-string, conversation type, etc.) plus the recency\ntie-breaker, so reviewers can see why the quick switcher orders results\nthe way it does without a debugger.\n\n* Log which search fields keep weak quick switcher matches\n\nExtend the developer-mode ranking debug so non-prefix results show\nthe member/channel field that matched (including whether it was the\ncurrent user), making cases like a Calls GM matching \"ac\" explainable.\n\nCo-authored-by: Joram Wilander <joram@mattermost.com>\n\n* Skip opaque DM/GM channel names when filtering quick switcher results\n\nDirect and group channel names are internal ids (userId__userId or a hex\nhash) that never appear in the UI. Matching the search term against them\ncould surface conversations that look unrelated, such as a Calls GM\nmatching \"ac\" only because those letters appear in its hash.\n\nCo-authored-by: Joram Wilander <joram@mattermost.com>\n\n* Remove temporary quick switcher ranking debug logging\n\nDrop the developer-mode ranking breakdown and match-attribution logging\nadded while diagnosing false GM/DM matches. The opaque channel-name\nfilter fix remains.\n\nCo-authored-by: Joram Wilander <joram@mattermost.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\nCo-authored-by: Joram Wilander <joram@mattermost.com>","tree":{"sha":"9024833c16ad73819face78666451d975a0fcb4b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ssamu04/txm-mattermost/git/trees/9024833c16ad73819face78666451d975a0fcb4b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ssamu04/txm-mattermost/git/commits/bef024abbe1c2f5c322ec7da869fe3e1355df50f","verification":{"payload":"tree 9024833c16ad73819face78666451d975a0fcb4b\nparent 3a1952f177c20091d47df53993a9cb98dbd3b5da\nauthor cursor[bot] <206951365+cursor[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1790010136 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790010136 -0400\n\n[MM-70519] Prioritize the DM with the matched person in the quick switcher (#38224)\n\n* [MM-70519] Prioritize DMs over GMs in the quick switcher\n\nThe \"Find Channels\" quick switcher merged its local results with the\nresults fetched from the server by appending the remote ones, so a\nperson the current user has never messaged directly was ranked below\nevery locally matched group message no matter how well the search term\nmatched their username. Rank the merged list as a whole instead, and\nderive the terms from the sorted items so they stay in lockstep.\n\nThe search prefix used for the \"starts with the search term\" ranking was\nalso compared verbatim against lower cased display names and usernames,\nso typing a capitalized name or a leading @ silently lost that ranking\nand fell back to recency, which favours chatty group messages.\n\nSorting the merged list means group messages hidden from the sidebar are\nno longer implicitly last, so demote them explicitly among otherwise\nequally relevant results.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* [MM-70519] Rank a DM above group messages containing the same person\n\nA group message matches a searched username only because one of its\nmembers is named that, and its display name is the member list in\nalphabetical order, so it looks like a prefix match whenever that member\nsorts first. Rank the direct message with the person ahead of those\ngroup messages, and cover the reported orderings with tests.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* [MM-70519] Derive group message names from member profiles in tests\n\nThe ranking fixtures set GM display names by hand while leaving\nprofilesInChannel empty, so the member names a GM is really matched on\nwere missing and two of the new assertions held without the fix. Build\nthe GMs from real member profiles the way the store does, and assert\nthat the merged items and terms stay in the same order.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* [MM-70519] Tighten the comments added to the quick switcher provider\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* [MM-70519] Retarget the Cypress quick switcher GM assertions\n\nTwo Cypress specs asserted that a group message was the SELECTED (top)\nresult when typing a member''s name, which is the ordering this ticket\nreports as a bug. Both tests are really about the group message being\nfindable that way - MM-T1226 by a name that is not displayed, MM-T3447_4\nby contrast with a closed group message - so assert that the group\nmessage is offered in the suggestion list rather than that it outranks\nthe person.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* Remove temporary test-review probe files committed by mistake\n\nThese two files were scratch jest probes used while reviewing the\nMM-70519 ranking tests and were never meant to land on the branch.\n\n* [MM-70519] Rank quick switcher results on one scale\n\nDemoting a GM only when compared against a DM left quickSwitchSorter\nwithout a consistent ordering: with a DM, a GM and an ordinary channel\nof intermediate recency all matching the same term, comparing any two of\nthem disagreed with comparing them through the third, so the result\ndepended on the order the local and server results happened to be\nconcatenated in. Two of the six input orders put the DM last, which is\nthe symptom this ticket is about.\n\nGive every result a rank on the same scale instead, and reach for\nrecency only when two results rank equally. A group message no longer\ncounts as starting with the search term at all, which is what actually\nmakes it weaker than the DM with the person: its display name is only\nits members listed alphabetically, so it starts with a searched username\npurely when that member sorts first. Ranking also removes an asymmetry\nin the old chain, where two open channels the user had never visited\ncompared as unequal in both directions.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* [MM-70519] Stop MM-T1243 assuming Town Square is adjacent to Off-Topic\n\nTyping \"T\" in the quick switcher now ranks prefix-matching users with\nthe channels instead of appending them, so one down-arrow no longer\nlands on Off-Topic. Drive the spec with two uniquely prefixed public\nchannels so it still covers click-out, arrow keys, and Enter.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* Address PR feedback: 0 answered, 2 resolved, 0 declined\n\n- Replace real people''s names in switch_channel_provider tests with fictional names\n- Extract named constants for the quick switcher ranking demotion weights\n\n* [MM-70519] Lock the quick switcher selection once the user engages\n\nGive suggestion_box a selection lock that is set only when the user\nexplicitly picks a row (arrow keys or hover). Until then the selection\ntracks the top result so incoming results are free to re-rank; once set,\nthe picked row stays selected as results merge in so it can''t be\nreordered out from under the user mid-selection. Typing releases the\nlock again.\n\n* [MM-70519] Rank quick switcher results by recency then conversation type\n\nFold an activity-recency band and a conversation-type order into the\nquick switcher ranking. Results opened within the last 30 days rank\nabove staler ones, which rank above never-opened conversations; within a\nband a DM outranks a GM, which outranks a channel. An exact but\nlong-abandoned DM now falls below recent GMs, a recently used DM stays\nabove them, and a never-messaged person sorts below any conversation the\nuser has actually opened.\n\n* [MM-70519] Rank prefix matches above mid-string matches in the quick switcher\n\nA channel directly named for the search term was ranking below direct\nmessages that only contained the term somewhere in the middle. Add a\nprefix-match tier to searchRank, below recency but above conversation\ntype, so a prefix-matching result (e.g. the Off-Topic channel) is not\nburied under DMs that merely mention the term.\n\n* Log quick switcher ranking breakdown in developer mode\n\nAdds a developer-mode-only console.table that prints, for each provided\nresult list, the per-result rank and the penalty breakdown (activity,\nprefix vs mid-string, conversation type, etc.) plus the recency\ntie-breaker, so reviewers can see why the quick switcher orders results\nthe way it does without a debugger.\n\n* Log which search fields keep weak quick switcher matches\n\nExtend the developer-mode ranking debug so non-prefix results show\nthe member/channel field that matched (including whether it was the\ncurrent user), making cases like a Calls GM matching \"ac\" explainable.\n\nCo-authored-by: Joram Wilander <joram@mattermost.com>\n\n* Skip opaque DM/GM channel names when filtering quick switcher results\n\nDirect and group channel names are internal ids (userId__userId or a hex\nhash) that never appear in the UI. Matching the search term against them\ncould surface conversations that look unrelated, such as a Calls GM\nmatching \"ac\" only because those letters appear in its hash.\n\nCo-authored-by: Joram Wilander <joram@mattermost.com>\n\n* Remove temporary quick switcher ranking debug logging\n\nDrop the developer-mode ranking breakdown and match-attribution logging\nadded while diagnosing false GM/DM matches. The opaque channel-name\nfilter fix remains.\n\nCo-authored-by: Joram Wilander <joram@mattermost.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\nCo-authored-by: Joram Wilander <joram@mattermost.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsWMYCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAZQEQAEwXCYNIv/L04EdJ4itU9xwp\n4IzwpDEEeFAnqq7JBkeukbGwPuqmqZtbCFpn3/l5wv+hVb43vWEVjAkj1+u9tSQL\nzF2ePSZuI2+ZTbk9G+l3RbzJ