arred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ssamu04/txm-mattermost/commit/3a1952f177c20091d47df53993a9cb98dbd3b5da","node_id":"C_kwDOUyPM59oAKDNhMTk1MmYxNzdjMjAwOTFkNDdkZjUzOTkzYTljYjk4ZGJkM2I1ZGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ssamu04/txm-mattermost/commit/1036970840a7e6a7c7ffac637c6e05e19ee72ee9","sha":"1036970840a7e6a7c7ffac637c6e05e19ee72ee9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ssamu04/txm-mattermost/commits/1036970840a7e6a7c7ffac637c6e05e19ee72ee9"}],"sha":"3a1952f177c20091d47df53993a9cb98dbd3b5da","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ssamu04/txm-mattermost/commits/3a1952f177c20091d47df53993a9cb98dbd3b5da"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1210556?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/cursor","id":206951365,"login":"cursor[bot]","node_id":"BOT_kgDODFXTxQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ssamu04/txm-mattermost/commits/1036970840a7e6a7c7ffac637c6e05e19ee72ee9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T14:32:06Z","email":"206951365+cursor[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"cursor[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T14:32:06Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"[MM-70289] Fix multi-byte (CJK) input in the AI Rewrite custom prompt (#38007)\n\n* [MM-70289] Fix CJK/IME input mangling in AI Rewrite custom prompt\n\nThe AI Rewrite custom prompt used a fully controlled Input, which\nre-asserts its value into the DOM on every render. When an unrelated\nre-render lands while an IME is still composing a multi-byte (CJK)\ncharacter, React overwrites the in-progress composition, so typing\nquickly drops, doubles, or splits characters (e.g. 글 -> 그ㄹ).\n\nIntroduce RewritePromptInput, an uncontrolled input that syncs its\nvalue imperatively (the same approach QuickInput uses for the message\nbox), so ongoing composition is never overwritten.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* [MM-70289] Strengthen AI Rewrite prompt IME tests\n\nAssert the onChange payload, cover onKeyDown forwarding (Enter submit)\nand function refs, add a value catch-up no-clobber case, and document\nthat the Playwright IME spec is a correctness guard while the unit test\nis the deterministic regression guard for the composition race.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* [MM-70289] Fix import order in rewrite Korean e2e spec\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* [MM-70289] Add Playwright test-docs JSDoc for rewrite Korean spec\n\nThe E2E Tests Check job failed because lint-test-docs requires a\nJSDoc @objective immediately above each new spec.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* [MM-70289] Keep rewrite prompt Input uncontrolled for IME\n\nThe shared Input widget always passed value={value} to the native\nelement. When callers omitted value and used defaultValue instead,\nReact still treated the field as controlled and re-asserted an empty\nstring on render, so CDP Hangul composition never stuck.\n\nOmit the native value prop when unset, skip RewritePromptInput''s\nimperative sync while composing, and assert the e2e prompt is focused\nbefore IME typing.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* [MM-70289] Retrigger CI after GitHub status API errors\n\nEnterprise CI/tests failed in update-initial-status with HttpError\nServer Error while posting the pending commit status. Tests never ran,\nso Enterprise CI/docker-image never published and E2E was not dispatched.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* [MM-70289] Retrigger CI now that GitHub is operational\n\nEnterprise CI/tests failed posting commit status during the 2026-08-17\nGitHub incident. GitHub now reports all systems operational; retrigger\nso Enterprise CI, docker-image, and E2E can run.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\nCo-authored-by: christopher <christopher@mattermost.com>","tree":{"sha":"122e07a5d505cd0834680ed74d6457a2f4b44a08","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ssamu04/txm-mattermost/git/trees/122e07a5d505cd0834680ed74d6457a2f4b44a08"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ssamu04/txm-mattermost/git/commits/1036970840a7e6a7c7ffac637c6e05e19ee72ee9","verification":{"payload":"tree 122e07a5d505cd0834680ed74d6457a2f4b44a08\nparent 1768b4ed7a21cdcdccb7eadf85c4fadcd8d129bb\nauthor cursor[bot] <206951365+cursor[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1790001126 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790001126 -0700\n\n[MM-70289] Fix multi-byte (CJK) input in the AI Rewrite custom prompt (#38007)\n\n* [MM-70289] Fix CJK/IME input mangling in AI Rewrite custom prompt\n\nThe AI Rewrite custom prompt used a fully controlled Input, which\nre-asserts its value into the DOM on every render. When an unrelated\nre-render lands while an IME is still composing a multi-byte (CJK)\ncharacter, React overwrites the in-progress composition, so typing\nquickly drops, doubles, or splits characters (e.g. 글 -> 그ㄹ).\n\nIntroduce RewritePromptInput, an uncontrolled input that syncs its\nvalue imperatively (the same approach QuickInput uses for the message\nbox), so ongoing composition is never overwritten.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* [MM-70289] Strengthen AI Rewrite prompt IME tests\n\nAssert the onChange payload, cover onKeyDown forwarding (Enter submit)\nand function refs, add a value catch-up no-clobber case, and document\nthat the Playwright IME spec is a correctness guard while the unit test\nis the deterministic regression guard for the composition race.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* [MM-70289] Fix import order in rewrite Korean e2e spec\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* [MM-70289] Add Playwright test-docs JSDoc for rewrite Korean spec\n\nThe E2E Tests Check job failed because lint-test-docs requires a\nJSDoc @objective immediately above each new spec.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* [MM-70289] Keep rewrite prompt Input uncontrolled for IME\n\nThe shared Input widget always passed value={value} to the native\nelement. When callers omitted value and used defaultValue instead,\nReact still treated the field as controlled and re-asserted an empty\nstring on render, so CDP Hangul composition never stuck.\n\nOmit the native value prop when unset, skip RewritePromptInput''s\nimperative sync while composing, and assert the e2e prompt is focused\nbefore IME typing.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* [MM-70289] Retrigger CI after GitHub status API errors\n\nEnterprise CI/tests failed in update-initial-status with HttpError\nServer Error while posting the pending commit status. Tests never ran,\nso Enterprise CI/docker-image never published and E2E was not dispatched.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* [MM-70289] Retrigger CI now that GitHub is operational\n\nEnterprise CI/tests failed posting commit status during the 2026-08-17\nGitHub incident. GitHub now reports all systems operational; retrigger\nso Enterprise CI, docker-image, and E2E can run.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\nCo-authored-by: christopher <christopher@mattermost.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsT/mCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAAj0QAJxQiz6yYIpAuXvJCJmq2fKj\nyOw0agxw364DsvO61uid2kOZ2SWAnuFrL4qNWO2daGu0ePDGdP4xiI6CG1EPgWqb\nBHHUsSAKjq8nR4P8dyy5FTCMHni3THo0/dwHsDB5WfmIwm+404bUfvPJFdNDZWlz\nGBNeh7rNI7ZVafTUQz7ObgJo5Ecdlb0ntv0qUoc072WUiAOKE6LzjwKfBhcskOHG\nYh6m9Mad7H5TummH/MoWBmD5d26YNePAM/mutCuuRARpWzYXuK7k2l5hgh904UeW\nnfVXChCcwp84cwhWXoQySi9DycuprbWwBTvQgIW2Oj1LqkXJWx8hpShYURbPkaAh\nTjZ5tbZ5X4Dtel2RcXmisYR7o0TDmtt4R2Ur6KmBaF1mnNLvB70lsb/+hmT26cqG\nT9sNu75HY+JF36Rx117nbDI5n8vwzsDDY92orfswFVfeqeZ5MzCj7IxYWJ/TxlzC\nsjsgXHzfoyekFRlEQR6CK3D+A7lfMe+pvMUahi8KkKo3qC4uPo2RLISW6e2eE6yD\nz+A6tF6OkMc4SaTfQ42jmCL2NKvMHRHHOQzmy8xUCfVCykaiRbAauB4jAfpOGl5k\n/Lz3RGhAkXHDr5NVMrhG433JSKugbJ8bVNFEN1OWDP6dHcNjhzgz/xutGuUrqcqQ\ndCZOBB9hQuppZk830Vay\n=sF2L\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T10:05:50Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://