/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JulienTant/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JulienTant/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JulienTant/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/JulienTant","id":785518,"login":"JulienTant","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4NTUxOA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JulienTant/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JulienTant/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JulienTant/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JulienTant/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JulienTant/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JulienTant","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ssamu04/txm-mattermost/commits/3db1a9adf80fd91d911de1b02632bd0bc3e9fe9d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T15:20:07Z","email":"785518+JulienTant@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Julien Tant"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T15:20:07Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"MM-70669: Migrate CPA fields into Global Attributes templates (#38537)\n\n* [MM-69869] Applies to: per-resource configuration (Users)\n\nAdds Profile display (attrs.visibility) and Who can set the value\n(attrs.managed) controls to the Users row of the Global Attributes\nApplies-to panel, reusing CPA''s existing value domain so both features\nstay compatible for a future migration. Webapp-only change; no backend\nmodifications.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Scope permission_values typing to the test that needs it\n\nThe shared PropertyField type doesn''t need permission_values/PermissionLevel --\nno production code in this feature reads or writes it (the design deliberately\nuses attrs.managed, not PermissionValues). Only one E2E regression test needed\nto read the raw field, so cast it locally there instead of widening the shared\ntype.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Simplify resource-interpolated error-kind check\n\nReplace the 5-way === chain with a Set lookup, module-scoped so it\nisn''t rebuilt every render.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix Prettier formatting in the e2e spec\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Rework Who-can-set-the-value layout to match design\n\nReplace RadioButtonGroup + per-option inline help text with a plain\nhorizontal radio row (Member / System Administrator, 16px gap) and a\nstatic caption below (8px gap), matching the design reference. Also\nsets explicit sizing (32px row min-height, 14px/20px option text) per\ndesign spec.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Update en.json for the renamed who_can_set help key\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Validate persisted attrs.visibility before use (CodeRabbit)\n\nAn unvalidated cast let an unexpected persisted value leave every\nProfile display segment unpressed, then round-trip that same bad\nvalue back to the server on Save. Falls back to when_set, matching\nthe defensive handling attrs.managed already gets two lines below.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix PermissionValues never taking effect for linked property fields\n\ncreatePropertyField unconditionally copied the template''s PermissionValues\n(always sysadmin) onto every new linked field, and PropertyFieldPatch had\nno slot to correct it afterward -- so \"Who can set the value\" had zero\nreal effect regardless of attrs.managed, for every linked field, not just\non unlock. Stop inheriting PermissionValues from the template on create,\nadd it to PropertyFieldPatch (member/sysadmin only, only for a field with\na LinkedFieldID), and wire the webapp to set it explicitly alongside\nattrs.managed in both directions.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Reject empty-but-non-nil LinkedFieldID in the PermissionValues patch guard\n\nPropertyField.IsValid only checks LinkedFieldID''s format when it''s\nnon-empty, so a caller sending linked_field_id: \"\" on create persists a\nnon-nil empty pointer -- the same degenerate value createPropertyField\nitself treats as \"not linked\" (LinkedFieldID != nil && *LinkedFieldID !=\n\"\"). The guard''s nil-only check missed this, letting it through as if\nlinked. Match the codebase''s existing linked-field convention.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix Prettier formatting in the e2e spec\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fall back to source template''s PermissionValues when a caller leaves it unset\n\nThe one caller that creates linked fields today (the managed CPA/access_control\ngroup) always resolves a PermissionValues via enforceGroupPermissions before this\nruns, so this is unreachable in practice. But any other property group using\nLinkedFieldID linking without that policy hook would otherwise get a permanently\nunconfigurable nil (PermissionField/PermissionOptions already inherit\nunconditionally) -- inheriting the template''s value here matches that existing\nbehavior instead, and nil already fails closed at the authorization layer either way.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Scrub ticket/plan/consumer-specific references from comments\n\nComments should be self-contained and, in shared PSAv2 infrastructure\n(property_field.go, the generic property-field API handlers), describe\nthe mechanism generically rather than citing one consumer (CPA, Global\nAttributes) as the reason a rule exists -- that rationale rots as other\nconsumers show up, and reads as false for anyone else using the same\ncode. Removes MM-69869/plans/ doc references throughout, drops the\nPropertyFieldPatch.PermissionValues struct comment entirely (the actual\nrule already lives at its enforcement point in patchPropertyField,\nmatching LinkedFieldID''s existing precedent of no struct-level comment),\nand rewords the patchPropertyField/test comments to explain the general\nweaker-PermissionField risk instead of citing CPA by name.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Minimize post-merge diff against master\n\nRevert the webapp PermissionLevel type back to master''s original\nPropertyPermissionLevel name/comment/domain (including its '''' sentinel),\nupdating our own call sites to match instead of carrying an unnecessary\nrename across shared code. Also drops a stray period added to a Go\ncomment during conflict resolution that isn''t in master.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* MM-70669: Migrate CPA fields into Global Attributes templates\n\nAdds a one-time startup migration that converts existing Custom Profile\nAttributes (User Attributes) fields into Global Attributes templates,\nso pre-existing CPA data gets feature parity with Global Attributes\nbefore that surface becomes the default. Flips FeatureFlags.GlobalAttributes\nto true and hides the legacy \"User Attributes\" console page behind it,\nwith the old page remaining reachable as a visibility-only fallback if\nthe flag is turned back off.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Modernize field-limit filler loop to range-over-int\n\ngolangci-lint (modernize/rangeint) flagged the counted for-loop as\nconvertible since the loop index isn''t used in the body.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix HA lost-update, ambiguous sibling links, and orphaned admin route\n\nMigrateLinkCPAFieldToGlobalAttributeTemplate blindly overwrote a field\nwithout optimistic concurrency, letting a rolling-restart node clobber\na concurrent admin edit from a still-live node. lookupReusableTemplate\ncould link two unrelated CPA fields to the same template when a name\ncollision''s \"_copy\" fallback matched another field''s literal name. The\nSystem Properties admin page and its feature-discovery sibling could\nboth end up hidden for a licensed, flag-on server, leaving the URL\nwith no registered route and silently redirecting elsewhere.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Remove the GlobalAttributes feature flag; simplify tests and comments\n\nThis migration is a one-way conversion with no rollback path, Global\nAttributes has never shipped, and several other in-flight features\nalready depend on it being on unconditionally. Keeping a flag around\nserved no purpose but added a third gating state that could leave an\nadmin console URL with no registered route.\n\nDeletes the now-permanently-superseded legacy \"User Attributes\" page\nand reverts its feature-discovery sibling to its pre-flag gate, which\nalso makes that routing-gap bug class structurally impossible instead\nof just guarded against. Cascades the removal through four e2e specs\nthat were toggling the flag for unrelated features, and fixes a\npre-existing test that still asserted the old flag-gated behavior.\n\nAlso: extracts a seedTemplate test helper (removing ~115 duplicated\nlines), trims comments down to essential context, aligns an\nidempotency-check idiom with its siblings, and classifies link\nfailures as permanent vs. retryable (mirroring the existing\ncreate-failure classifier) so a deterministically-invalid legacy field\ncan no longer block the whole migration''s completion marker forever.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Guarantee template name disambiguation never fails\n\nReplaces the fixed \"_copy\" suffix with the CPA field''s own ID, which\ncan never collide with anything (including another feature''s reserved\ntemplate name), eliminating two permanent-skip paths: a second\ncollision on the disambiguated name, and a name reserved by another\nfeature. Also stops the \" (copy)\" display_name suffix from turning an\nalready near-limit name into its own permanent skip by skipping the\nsuffix instead of failing when it would overflow.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix CI: missing mock expectation and e2e implicit-any type\n\ntestlib.GetMockStoreForSetupFunctions hand-lists an expected\nGetByName call for every migration key so mock-store-backed tests can\nboot a server without hitting the real store. The new CPA-to-Global-\nAttributes migration key was missing from that list, so any test\nusing SetupWithStoreMock/SetupEnterpriseWithStoreMock panicked with\n\"mock: Unexpected Method Call\" during server startup — cascading into\ndozens of unrelated failures across the Postgres, Elasticsearch,\nOpenSearch, and Enterprise CI jobs.\n\nAlso fixes two implicit-any parameters in\nglobal_attributes_listing.spec.ts that tripped the e2e tsc check.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Redirect the legacy User Attributes URL to Manage Attributes\n\nRemoving the GlobalAttributes flag reverted user_attributes_feature_discovery''s\nisHidden back to a plain Enterprise+ check, leaving system_attributes/user_attributes\nwith no matching subsection on Enterprise+ licenses -- the admin console silently\nfell through to an unrelated default page. Add a redirect subsection covering the\ncomplementary license range, restore the isHidden invariant test, and point the two\ne2e specs that clicked the old sidebar link at Attribute Management instead.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Slugify legacy CPA field names that aren''t CEL-safe\n\nA CPA field''s Name predating the CEL-safe-identifier rule (e.g. containing\na space, or a bare reserved word like \"in\") previously failed template\ncreation deterministically and was permanently skipped, since the legacy\neditor that could otherwise manage it is gone. Slugify such a name into a\nCEL-safe template name instead -- mirroring the webapp''s existing slugify\nutility -- so these fields migrate like everything else. The field''s own\nName and display_name are left untouched.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Handle a trailing slash in the legacy User Attributes redirect\n\nThe admin console''s routes match by prefix, not exact path, so\n/system_attributes/user_attributes/ (trailing slash) also reaches this\ncomponent -- but the regex anchored on \"user_attributes$\" wouldn''t match\nthat string, so the redirect was a no-op and left the user on the dead\nlegacy URL.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix flaky Rank popover reorder step in the e2e attribute form test\n\nThe Rank submenu (components/menu/sub_menu.tsx) opens on mouseenter and\ncloses as soon as the pointer leaves its trigger, with no grace period.\nClicking the nested rank option forced the mouse off the trigger to reach\nit, racing the submenu''s close and detaching the item mid-click -- this\nwas failing consistently in CI (playwright-full, all 4 enterprise/upgrade\nvariants). Open the submenu with hover, then select the item via keyboard\nso the pointer never leaves the trigger.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix ambiguous textbox locator in the AD/LDAP external source e2e test\n\ngetByRole(''textbox'') with no scope also matched the admin sidebar''s\n\"Find settings\" filter and the Display name input already on the page,\nthrowing a strict-mode violation instead of filling the LDAP modal''s\nown input. This was failing consistently in CI (playwright-full,\nmultiple enterprise/upgrade variants). Scope to the AttributeModal\ndialog once it''s visible.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Skip the resource-picker test when ChannelAttributes is off\n\nThe Channels resource type is additionally gated behind the\nChannelAttributes flag (attribute_details.tsx), on top of the\nEnterprise-tier license requireGlobalAttributesEnabled already checks.\nAn environment where the flag is off (e.g. a server upgraded from an\nolder release whose config predates the flag) only offers Users and\nPosts, deterministically failing the 3-item assertion -- this was\nfailing consistently in CI''s upgrade-from-release e2e variants.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Skip the two remaining Channels-dependent applies-to tests when off\n\nSame gap as the previous commit: \"removes a pending resource locally\"\nand \"saves the template plus one linked field per selected resource\"\nboth click the Channels menu item via the UI picker, gated behind the\nsame ChannelAttributes flag. This file runs in serial mode, so each of\nthese was only reachable -- and only actually exercised in CI -- once\nan earlier failure in the file got fixed, which is why they hadn''t\nsurfaced as their own CI failures yet.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Read the CPA-to-Global-Attributes candidate list from master\n\nSearchPropertyFields unconditionally read from the replica, with no\ncontext parameter to override it -- unlike its sibling PropertyFieldStore\nmethods (Get, GetMany, GetFieldByName, GetForGroup), which already accept\nan rctx for exactly this. Since this migration is one-shot with no\nperiodic re-scan, a CPA field missed here due to replica lag would be\npermanently invisible to it, not just delayed.\n\nAdds rctx to SearchPropertyFields across the store interface and its two\ngenerated layers (regenerated via `make layers`/`make store-mocks`, not\nhand-edited), threads it through PropertyService''s internal wrapper, and\nhas the migration''s own call force a master read via\nstore.RequestContextWithMaster. All other ~30 existing callers are\nunaffected: HasMaster defaults to false, so they keep reading from the\nreplica exactly as before, and the public Plugin API surface doesn''t\nchange signature at all.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Remove orphaned system_properties translation keys\n\nadmin.system_properties.user_properties.subtitle/.title had no source\nstrings left after system_properties.tsx was removed earlier in this\nbranch, but 10 locale files still carried stale translations for them.\nmake i18n-extract cleans these up; en.json itself was already in sync.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix stale ''Edit attribute'' heading assertion in e2e test\n\nattribute_details.tsx''s editTitle changed from a static \"Edit attribute\"\nto a dynamic \"Edit {name} Attribute\" in PR #38535 (merged into master\ntoday), but that PR didn''t update this test to match. Only surfaced\nonce we merged master into this branch, since our own commits never\ntouched this component.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix two flaky e2e specs: mobile RHS menu race and display-name truncation\n\nmobile_rhs_focus.spec.ts: wait for the mobile navbar''s channel menu button\nto render before opening it. Right after page load the app can still be\nsettling into mobile layout, so opening the menu too early races the\nheader page object''s one-shot visibility check, which falls back to the\ndesktop header''s copy of the button -- permanently hidden at this\nviewport width -- and times out.\n\nglobal_attributes_form.spec.ts: shorten the display name in \"rolls back a\npartial save and lets the admin retry successfully\" so it stays under the\nDisplay name input''s 40-char maxLength. The full name silently truncated\nserver-side, so the test''s own hand-computed expected name never matched\nwhat was actually persisted.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Restore the Classification Markings row''s read-only subtitle and CPA field permission defaults\n\nglobal_attributes_table.tsx/.scss: PR #38535 accidentally deleted\nAttributeCell''s classification-row subtitle block (and its supporting\nmessage/CSS) while polishing unrelated channel-attribute UI, silently\nbreaking the pre-existing e2e assertion that it renders. Restore it,\nmatching the component''s own pre-removal implementation exactly.\n\nglobal_attributes_table.test.tsx: the same PR \"fixed\" the failing unit\ntest by flipping its assertion to expect the subtitle absent, instead of\nnoticing the regression. Restore the original positive assertion.\n\nglobal_attributes_listing.spec.ts: the row''s dot-menu (offering Edit to\nthe classification attribute page) only appears when that page is\nactually reachable (Enterprise Advanced tier + ChannelAttributes flag) --\na legitimate feature added after this test was written. Compute\nreachability the same way the component does instead of assuming the\ndot-menu is always absent.\n\ncustom_profile_attributes.go: createCPAField never set PermissionField/\nPermissionValues/PermissionOptions, unlike the generic property-field API.\nLeft nil, SessionHasPermissionToSetPropertyFieldValues denies everyone --\nincluding sysadmin -- from ever setting that field''s value. Nil-fill with\nthe same default the generic API uses.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix post-merge fallout: correct CPA PermissionValues default, update hook config call\n\ncustom_profile_attributes.go: master''s PR #38119 split PermissionValues\ndefaulting into its own DefaultPropertyFieldValuesPermissionLevel (system\nTargetType no longer forces sysadmin there, unlike Field/Options). Our fix\nwas still using the single, now-Field/Options-only default, which pinned\nCPA field values to sysadmin and locked out regular members setting their\nown values. Switch PermissionValues to the correct helper.\n\nmigrations_test.go: NewAccessControlAttributeValidationHook took a plain\nPermissionChecker before the merge; master''s PR #38119 changed it to a\nconfig struct. Update our test call to match.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8ae12becc3555e74e3bf3908919b670593caa262","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ssamu04/txm-mattermost/git/trees/8ae12becc3555e74e3bf3908919b670593caa262"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ssamu04/txm-mattermost/git/commits/3db1a9adf80fd91d911de1b02632bd0bc3e9fe9d","verification":{"payload":"tree 8ae12becc3555e74e3bf3908919b670593caa262\nparent d4d4e42a7a0755a207e36d3c6916df9e962e0ed5\nauthor Julien Tant <785518+JulienTant@users.noreply.github.com> 1789658407 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789658407 -0700\n\nMM-70669: Migrate CPA fields into Global Attributes templates (#38537)\n\n* [MM-69869] Applies to: per-resource configuration (Users)\n\nAdds Profile display (attrs.visibility) and Who can set the value\n(attrs.managed) controls to the Users row of the Global Attributes\nApplies-to panel, reusing CPA''s existing value domain so both features\nstay compatible for a future migration. Webapp-only change; no backend\nmodifications.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Scope permission_values typing to the test that needs it\n\nThe shared PropertyField type doesn''t need permission_values/PermissionLevel --\nno production code in this feature reads or writes it (the design deliberately\nuses attrs.managed, not PermissionValues). Only one E2E regression test needed\nto read the raw field, so cast it locally there instead of widening the shared\ntype.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Simplify resource-interpolated error-kind check\n\nReplace the 5-way === chain with a Set lookup, module-scoped so it\nisn''t rebuilt every render.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix Prettier formatting in the e2e spec\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Rework Who-can-set-the-value layout to match design\n\nReplace RadioButtonGroup + per-option inline help text with a plain\nhorizontal radio row (Member / System Administrator, 16px gap) and a\nstatic caption below (8px gap), matching the design reference. Also\nsets explicit sizing (32px row min-height, 14px/20px option text) per\ndesign spec.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Update en.json for the renamed who_can_set help key\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Validate persisted attrs.visibility before use (CodeRabbit)\n\nAn unvalidated cast let an unexpected persisted value leave every\nProfile display segment unpressed, then round-trip that same bad\nvalue back to the server on Save. Falls back to when_set, matching\nthe defensive handling attrs.managed already gets two lines below.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix PermissionValues never taking effect for linked property fields\n\ncreatePropertyField unconditionally copied the template''s PermissionValues\n(always sysadmin) onto every new linked field, and PropertyFieldPatch had\nno slot to correct it afterward -- so \"Who can set the value\" had zero\nreal effect regardless of attrs.managed, for every linked field, not just\non unlock. Stop inheriting PermissionValues from the template on create,\nadd it to PropertyFieldPatch (member/sysadmin only, only for a field with\na LinkedFieldID), and wire the webapp to set it explicitly alongside\nattrs.managed in both directions.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Reject empty-but-non-nil LinkedFieldID in the PermissionValues patch guard\n\nPropertyField.IsValid only checks LinkedFieldID''s format when it''s\nnon-empty, so a caller sending linked_field_id: \"\" on create persists a\nnon-nil empty pointer -- the same degenerate value createPropertyField\nitself treats as \"not linked\" (LinkedFieldID != nil && *LinkedFieldID !=\n\"\"). The guard''s nil-only check missed this, letting it through as if\nlinked. Match the codebase''s existing linked-field convention.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix Prettier formatting in the e2e spec\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fall back to source template''s PermissionValues when a caller leaves it unset\n\nThe one caller that creates linked fields today (the managed CPA/access_control\ngroup) always resolves a PermissionValues via enforceGroupPermissions before this\nruns, so this is unreachable in practice. But any other property group using\nLinkedFieldID linking without that policy hook would otherwise get a permanently\nunconfigurable nil (PermissionField/PermissionOptions already inherit\nunconditionally) -- inheriting the template''s value here matches that existing\nbehavior instead, and nil already fails closed at the authorization layer either way.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Scrub ticket/plan/consumer-specific references from comments\n\nComments should be self-contained and, in shared PSAv2 infrastructure\n(property_field.go, the generic property-field API handlers), describe\nthe mechanism generically rather than citing one consumer (CPA, Global\nAttributes) as the reason a rule exists -- that rationale rots as other\nconsumers show up, and reads as false for anyone else using the same\ncode. Removes MM-69869/plans/ doc references throughout, drops the\nPropertyFieldPatch.PermissionValues struct comment entirely (the actual\nrule already lives at its enforcement point in patchPropertyField,\nmatching LinkedFieldID''s existing precedent of no struct-level comment),\nand rewords the patchPropertyField/test comments to explain the general\nweaker-PermissionField risk instead of citing CPA by name.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Minimize post-merge diff against master\n\nRevert the webapp PermissionLevel type back to master''s original\nPropertyPermissionLevel name/comment/domain (including its '''' sentinel),\nupdating our own call sites to match instead of carrying an unnecessary\nrename across shared code. Also drops a stray period added to a Go\ncomment during conflict resolution that isn''t in master.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* MM-70669: Migrate CPA fields into Global Attributes templates\n\nAdds a one-time startup migration that converts existing Custom Profile\nAttributes (User Attributes) fields into Global Attributes templates,\nso pre-existing CPA data gets feature parity with Global Attributes\nbefore that surface becomes the default. Flips FeatureFlags.GlobalAttributes\nto true and hides the legacy \"User Attributes\" console page behind it,\nwith the old page remaining reachable as a visibility-only fallback if\nthe flag is turned back off.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Modernize field-limit filler loop to range-over-int\n\ngolangci-lint (modernize/rangeint) flagged the counted for-loop as\nconvertible since the loop index isn''t used in the body.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix HA lost-update, ambiguous sibling links, and orphaned admin route\n\nMigrateLinkCPAFieldToGlobalAttributeTemplate blindly overwrote a field\nwithout optimistic concurrency, letting a rolling-restart node clobber\na concurrent admin edit from a still-live node. lookupReusableTemplate\ncould link two unrelated CPA fields to the same template when a name\ncollision''s \"_copy\" fallback matched another field''s literal name. The\nSystem Properties admin page and its feature-discovery sibling could\nboth end up hidden for a licensed, flag-on server, leaving the URL\nwith no registered route and silently redirecting elsewhere.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Remove the GlobalAttributes feature flag; simplify tests and comments\n\nThis migration is a one-way conversion with no rollback path, Global\nAttributes has never shipped, and several other in-flight features\nalready depend on it being on unconditionally. Keeping a flag around\nserved no purpose but added a third gating state that could leave an\nadmin console URL with no registered route.\n\nDeletes the now-permanently-superseded legacy \"User Attributes\" page\nand reverts its feature-discovery sibling to its pre-flag gate, which\nalso makes that routing-gap bug class structurally impossible instead\nof just guarded against. Cascades the removal through four e2e specs\nthat were toggling the flag for unrelated features, and fixes a\npre-existing test that still asserted the old flag-gated behavior.\n\nAlso: extracts a seedTemplate test helper (removing ~115 duplicated\nlines), trims comments down to essential context, aligns an\nidempotency-check idiom with its siblings, and classifies link\nfailures as permanent vs. retryable (mirroring the existing\ncreate-failure classifier) so a deterministically-invalid legacy field\ncan no longer block the whole migration''s completion marker forever.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Guarantee template name disambiguation never fails\n\nReplaces the fixed \"_copy\" suffix with the CPA field''s own ID, which\ncan never collide with anything (including another feature''s reserved\ntemplate name), eliminating two permanent-skip paths: a second\ncollision on the disambiguated name, and a name reserved by another\nfeature. Also stops the \" (copy)\" display_name suffix from turning an\nalready near-limit name into its own permanent skip by skipping the\nsuffix instead of failing when it would overflow.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix CI: missing mock expectation and e2e implicit-any type\n\ntestlib.GetMockStoreForSetupFunctions hand-lists an expected\nGetByName call for every migration key so mock-store-backed tests can\nboot a server without hitting the real store. The new CPA-to-Global-\nAttributes migration key was missing from that list, so any test\nusing SetupWithStoreMock/SetupEnterpriseWithStoreMock panicked with\n\"mock: Unexpected Method Call\" during server startup — cascading into\ndozens of unrelated failures across the Postgres, Elasticsearch,\nOpenSearch, and Enterprise CI jobs.\n\nAlso fixes two implicit-any parameters in\nglobal_attributes_listing.spec.ts that tripped the e2e tsc check.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Redirect the legacy User Attributes URL to Manage Attributes\n\nRemoving the GlobalAttributes flag reverted user_attributes_feature_discovery''s\nisHidden back to a plain Enterprise+ check, leaving system_attributes/user_attributes\nwith no matching subsection on Enterprise+ licenses -- the admin console silently\nfell through to an unrelated default page. Add a redirect subsection covering the\ncomplementary license range, restore the isHidden invariant test, and point the two\ne2e specs that clicked the old sidebar link at Attribute Management instead.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Slugify legacy CPA field names that aren''t CEL-safe\n\nA CPA field''s Name predating the CEL-safe-identifier rule (e.g. containing\na space, or a bare reserved word like \"in\") previously failed template\ncreation deterministically and was permanently skipped, since the legacy\neditor that could otherwise manage it is gone. Slugify such a name into a\nCEL-safe template name instead -- mirroring the webapp''s existing slugify\nutility -- so these fields migrate like everything else. The field''s own\nName and display_name are left untouched.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Handle a trailing slash in the legacy User Attributes redirect\n\nThe admin console''s routes match by prefix, not exact path, so\n/system_attributes/user_attributes/ (trailing slash) also reaches this\ncomponent -- but the regex anchored on \"user_attributes$\" wouldn''t match\nthat string, so the redirect was a no-op and left the user on the dead\nlegacy URL.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix flaky Rank popover reorder step in the e2e attribute form test\n\nThe Rank submenu (components/menu/sub_menu.tsx) opens on mouseenter and\ncloses as soon as the pointer leaves its trigger, with no grace period.\nClicking the nested rank option forced the mouse off the trigger to reach\nit, racing the submenu''s close and detaching the item mid-click -- this\nwas failing consistently in CI (playwright-full, all 4 enterprise/upgrade\nvariants). Open the submenu with hover, then select the item via keyboard\nso the pointer never leaves the trigger.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix ambiguous textbox locator in the AD/LDAP external source e2e test\n\ngetByRole(''textbox'') with no scope also matched the admin sidebar''s\n\"Find settings\" filter and the Display name input already on the page,\nthrowing a strict-mode violation instead of filling the LDAP modal''s\nown input. This was failing consistently in CI (playwright-full,\nmultiple enterprise/upgrade variants). Scope to the AttributeModal\ndialog once it''s visible.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Skip the resource-picker test when ChannelAttributes is off\n\nThe Channels resource type is additionally gated behind the\nChannelAttributes flag (attribute_details.tsx), on top of the\nEnterprise-tier license requireGlobalAttributesEnabled already checks.\nAn environment where the flag is off (e.g. a server upgraded from an\nolder release whose config predates the flag) only offers Users and\nPosts, deterministically failing the 3-item assertion -- this was\nfailing consistently in CI''s upgrade-from-release e2e variants.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Skip the two remaining Channels-dependent applies-to tests when off\n\nSame gap as the previous commit: \"removes a pending resource locally\"\nand \"saves the template plus one linked field per selected resource\"\nboth click the Channels menu item via the UI picker, gated behind the\nsame ChannelAttributes flag. This file runs in serial mode, so each of\nthese was only reachable -- and only actually exercised in CI -- once\nan earlier failure in the file got fixed, which is why they hadn''t\nsurfaced as their own CI failures yet.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Read the CPA-to-Global-Attributes candidate list from master\n\nSearchPropertyFields unconditionally read from the replica, with no\ncontext parameter to override it -- unlike its sibling PropertyFieldStore\nmethods (Get, GetMany, GetFieldByName, GetForGroup), which already accept\nan rctx for exactly this. Since this migration is one-shot with no\nperiodic re-scan, a CPA field missed here due to replica lag would be\npermanently invisible to it, not just delayed.\n\nAdds rctx to SearchPropertyFields across the store interface and its two\ngenerated layers (regenerated via `make layers`/`make store-mocks`, not\nhand-edited), threads it through PropertyService''s internal wrapper, and\nhas the migration''s own call force a master read via\nstore.RequestContextWithMaster. All other ~30 existing callers are\nunaffected: HasMaster defaults to false, so they keep reading from the\nreplica exactly as before, and the public Plugin API surface doesn''t\nchange signature at all.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Remove orphaned system_properties translation keys\n\nadmin.system_properties.user_properties.subtitle/.title had no source\nstrings left after system_properties.tsx was removed earlier in this\nbranch, but 10 locale files still carried stale translations for them.\nmake i18n-extract cleans these up; en.json itself was already in sync.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix stale ''Edit attribute'' heading assertion in e2e test\n\nattribute_details.tsx''s editTitle changed from a static \"Edit attribute\"\nto a dynamic \"Edit {name} Attribute\" in PR #38535 (merged into master\ntoday), but that PR didn''t update this test to match. Only surfaced\nonce we merged master into this branch, since our own commits never\ntouched this component.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix two flaky e2e specs: mobile RHS menu race and display-name truncation\n\nmobile_rhs_focus.spec.ts: wait for the mobile navbar''s channel menu button\nto render before opening it. Right after page load the app can still be\nsettling into mobile layout, so opening the menu too early races the\nheader page object''s one-shot visibility check, which falls back to the\ndesktop header''s copy of the button -- permanently hidden at this\nviewport width -- and times out.\n\nglobal_attributes_form.spec.ts: shorten the display name in \"rolls back a\npartial save and lets the admin retry successfully\" so it stays under the\nDisplay name input''s 40-char maxLength. The full name silently truncated\nserver-side, so the test''s own hand-computed expected name never matched\nwhat was actually persisted.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Restore the Classification Markings row''s read-only subtitle and CPA field permission defaults\n\nglobal_attributes_table.tsx/.scss: PR #38535 accidentally deleted\nAttributeCell''s classification-row subtitle block (and its supporting\nmessage/CSS) while polishing unrelated channel-attribute UI, silently\nbreaking the pre-existing e2e assertion that it renders. Restore it,\nmatching the component''s own pre-removal implementation exactly.\n\nglobal_attributes_table.test.tsx: the same PR \"fixed\" the failing unit\ntest by flipping its assertion to expect the subtitle absent, instead of\nnoticing the regression. Restore the original positive assertion.\n\nglobal_attributes_listing.spec.ts: the row''s dot-menu (offering Edit to\nthe classification attribute page) only appears when that page is\nactually reachable (Enterprise Advanced tier + ChannelAttributes flag) --\na legitimate feature added after this test was written. Compute\nreachability the same way the component does instead of assuming the\ndot-menu is always absent.\n\ncustom_profile_attributes.go: createCPAField never set PermissionField/\nPermissionValues/PermissionOptions, unlike the generic property-field API.\nLeft nil, SessionHasPermissionToSetPropertyFieldValues denies everyone --\nincluding sysadmin -- from ever setting that field''s value. Nil-fill with\nthe same default the generic API uses.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix post-merge fallout: correct CPA PermissionValues default, update hook config call\n\ncustom_profile_attributes.go: master''s PR #38119 split PermissionValues\ndefaulting into its own DefaultPropertyFieldValuesPermissionLevel (system\nTargetType no longer forces sysadmin there, unlike Field/Options). Our fix\nwas still using the single, now-Field/Options-only default, which pinned\nCPA field values to sysadmin and locked out regular members setting their\nown values. Switch PermissionValues to the correct helper.\n\nmigrations_test.go: NewAccessControlAttributeValidationHook took a plain\nPermissionChecker before the merge; master''s PR #38119 changed it to a\nconfig struct. Update our test call to match.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqrAUnCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAziIQAIZVezm8Q9ars7/z84ZUQ85Z\n9FFlYmtjz27LlvFKweurbIHRxrPkSVkqUGBopFaTYGvnVCG2BiKgu8FtWhFcngIf\nKs7mLjlX+lVj4CPpFALFtK/cnXt62b8Axj3spUvyaal55Dshgez8f3mX2L6SOX9h\n8ZKf3yR2kStZ3XlHHm6hJ+0YRiAWEY3CAYnywPhr7CbG74f6iV/zmLGuqHO+926j\nGTK6b07jmj2PL7DO5RZK0WrCM7kuxe6geNZ4Yicy99NnKZHI6yzJSg22Ywnm142x\n8XrlqmoKqzzD3BehPgONN6TH67R9nCNQbsH+WBNbojPRv91iCcr7PEflYEr1nVcP\nVtqRpaxQLBhrMX6wWr5GnENy6sVEnbXUeQGTW+L5ndC39vSV60+IiLqOh9eq9xkB\nwko/VUkay1OIkvBVZ5v0/SnVVlf+dk6GGnLvJBzLr8k6O4aIz86oIIyKF6DCVV0u\ni8TYwlkTlzR6SNzCAh831hgn