rs/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ssamu04/txm-mattermost/commit/fc07d7087d4efab3fa98f822c6bf22ea37f63473","node_id":"C_kwDOUyPM59oAKGZjMDdkNzA4N2Q0ZWZhYjNmYTk4ZjgyMmM2YmYyMmVhMzdmNjM0NzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ssamu04/txm-mattermost/commit/62f57271740726da92dda34cbfefdf9aff587e3b","sha":"62f57271740726da92dda34cbfefdf9aff587e3b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ssamu04/txm-mattermost/commits/62f57271740726da92dda34cbfefdf9aff587e3b"}],"sha":"fc07d7087d4efab3fa98f822c6bf22ea37f63473","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ssamu04/txm-mattermost/commits/fc07d7087d4efab3fa98f822c6bf22ea37f63473"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16541325?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hanzei/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hanzei/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hanzei/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hanzei/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hanzei","id":16541325,"login":"hanzei","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTQxMzI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hanzei/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hanzei/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hanzei/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hanzei/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hanzei/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hanzei","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ssamu04/txm-mattermost/commits/62f57271740726da92dda34cbfefdf9aff587e3b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T12:54:46Z","email":"ben.schumacher@mattermost.com","name":"Ben Schumacher"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T12:54:46Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"[MM-70617] Add webapp support for user-owned bot PAT expiry (#37604)\n\n* Add bot PAT expiry support to webapp\n\nCo-authored-by: Ben Schumacher <hanzei@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Add copy action for generated bot tokens\n\nCo-authored-by: Ben Schumacher <hanzei@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Clarify Add Bot default token expiry UX\n\nCo-authored-by: Ben Schumacher <hanzei@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Address bot PAT expiry review feedback\n\nCo-authored-by: Ben Schumacher <hanzei@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Rename PAT expiry instance helpers\n\nCo-authored-by: Ben Schumacher <hanzei@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Update non-compliant token bot copy\n\nCo-authored-by: Ben Schumacher <hanzei@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Clarify plugin-owned bot token exemption\n\nCo-authored-by: Ben Schumacher <hanzei@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Update bot token Cypress test for disabled save\n\nCo-authored-by: Ben Schumacher <hanzei@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Remove accidental duplicate protected-system-bot tests from merge\n\nThe master merge produced two copies of the protected-system-bot test\npair; the first lacked the maxLifetimeDays prop required after the PAT\nexpiry changes, failing the TS build.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Don''t orphan the bot when its default token is rejected\n\ncreateBot has already succeeded by the time createUserAccessToken runs, so\nreturning to the form left a bot behind that a retry could not recreate.\nRoles are now applied and the user lands on the bot list either way; the\nexpiry itself is already validated before createBot.\n\nAlso reset MaximumPersonalAccessTokenLifetimeDays after the expiry spec:\ninitSetup''s config patch omits the key, so the cap leaked into later specs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Share one expiry picker across the token forms\n\nThe select, custom-date input and policy hints existed in three copies\n(user settings, Add Bot, bot token rows) and had already drifted: the bot\ncopies put <FormattedMessage> inside <option>, where children must be a\nstring. Layout still differs per call site, so only the control itself moves\ninto the shared component; each caller keeps its own label and wrapper.\n\nThe helpers move to components/common/token_expiry_picker/token_expiry so the\nshared component doesn''t import the section that renders it, and\nuser_access_token_section re-exports them for existing importers.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Wait for the bot owner before rendering the bot list\n\nA resolved owner profile is what marks a bot user-owned, and the fetch was\nfire-and-forget, so rows could render as plugin-owned: no expiry control, yet\nSave enabled. With a maximum lifetime configured the server then rejected the\ntoken as expires_at_required with no control on screen to satisfy it.\n\nThe request was already in flight, so awaiting it adds no round trip, and\ngetUser resolves with {error} rather than rejecting when owner_id is a plugin id.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Exempt system-owned bots from the token expiry policy\n\nTheir OwnerId is a real sysadmin, so resolving the owner marks them user-owned\nand enforces an expiry the server exempts them from. system_owned is the flag\nfor this, and the server''s resolveBotOwner now keys off IsSystemOwned too, so\nboth sides cover system-bot and the content-flagging bot alike.\n\nThe existing protected-bot tests only ran with no policy configured.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>\nCo-authored-by: Ben Schumacher <hanzei@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"28d6b48cbc3c0248436138029b56d10d794d5b16","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ssamu04/txm-mattermost/git/trees/28d6b48cbc3c0248436138029b56d10d794d5b16"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ssamu04/txm-mattermost/git/commits/62f57271740726da92dda34cbfefdf9aff587e3b","verification":{"payload":"tree 28d6b48cbc3c0248436138029b56d10d794d5b16\nparent c6175dfd82b9801fe8c1622839c703ee6a3b4f65\nauthor Ben Schumacher <ben.schumacher@mattermost.com> 1789649686 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789649686 +0200\n\n[MM-70617] Add webapp support for user-owned bot PAT expiry (#37604)\n\n* Add bot PAT expiry support to webapp\n\nCo-authored-by: Ben Schumacher <hanzei@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Add copy action for generated bot tokens\n\nCo-authored-by: Ben Schumacher <hanzei@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Clarify Add Bot default token expiry UX\n\nCo-authored-by: Ben Schumacher <hanzei@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Address bot PAT expiry review feedback\n\nCo-authored-by: Ben Schumacher <hanzei@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Rename PAT expiry instance helpers\n\nCo-authored-by: Ben Schumacher <hanzei@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Update non-compliant token bot copy\n\nCo-authored-by: Ben Schumacher <hanzei@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Clarify plugin-owned bot token exemption\n\nCo-authored-by: Ben Schumacher <hanzei@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Update bot token Cypress test for disabled save\n\nCo-authored-by: Ben Schumacher <hanzei@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Remove accidental duplicate protected-system-bot tests from merge\n\nThe master merge produced two copies of the protected-system-bot test\npair; the first lacked the maxLifetimeDays prop required after the PAT\nexpiry changes, failing the TS build.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Don''t orphan the bot when its default token is rejected\n\ncreateBot has already succeeded by the time createUserAccessToken runs, so\nreturning to the form left a bot behind that a retry could not recreate.\nRoles are now applied and the user lands on the bot list either way; the\nexpiry itself is already validated before createBot.\n\nAlso reset MaximumPersonalAccessTokenLifetimeDays after the expiry spec:\ninitSetup''s config patch omits the key, so the cap leaked into later specs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Share one expiry picker across the token forms\n\nThe select, custom-date input and policy hints existed in three copies\n(user settings, Add Bot, bot token rows) and had already drifted: the bot\ncopies put <FormattedMessage> inside <option>, where children must be a\nstring. Layout still differs per call site, so only the control itself moves\ninto the shared component; each caller keeps its own label and wrapper.\n\nThe helpers move to components/common/token_expiry_picker/token_expiry so the\nshared component doesn''t import the section that renders it, and\nuser_access_token_section re-exports them for existing importers.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Wait for the bot owner before rendering the bot list\n\nA resolved owner profile is what marks a bot user-owned, and the fetch was\nfire-and-forget, so rows could render as plugin-owned: no expiry control, yet\nSave enabled. With a maximum lifetime configured the server then rejected the\ntoken as expires_at_required with no control on screen to satisfy it.\n\nThe request was already in flight, so awaiting it adds no round trip, and\ngetUser resolves with {error} rather than rejecting when owner_id is a plugin id.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Exempt system-owned bots from the token expiry policy\n\nTheir OwnerId is a real sysadmin, so resolving the owner marks them user-owned\nand enforces an expiry the server exempts them from. system_owned is the flag\nfor this, and the server''s resolveBotOwner now keys off IsSystemOwned too, so\nboth sides cover system-bot and the content-flagging bot 