s_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hatlabs/signalk-alert-rules/commits/c1199a24e791b615d8fef2d4ad367a16ff7e3463/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T21:06:02Z","email":"matti.airas@hatlabs.fi","name":"Matti Airas"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T07:19:05Z","email":"matti.airas@hatlabs.fi","name":"Matti Airas"},"message":"refactor: drop the detector clear delay\n\nA sustained or outside detector keeps duration and hysteresis; its\nalert ends as soon as the value is back past the limit by the margin.\nA detector saved with clearDuration is refused. The editor loses the\nClear delay field, and the steps summary and rule detail word only\nthe margin.\n\nWith no timer running toward a clear, a timer''s progress always runs\ntoward setting, so Progress drops its direction.\n\nThe two examples that set a 30 s clear delay drop it, and their\nscenarios clear when the value is back.\n\nRefs https://github.com/hatlabs/signalk-alert-rules/issues/176\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01R6kYxcPmrzvZAn5kE3B8wh","tree":{"sha":"3e4466c250b0aae377729719b9ca838ef639a59a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hatlabs/signalk-alert-rules/git/trees/3e4466c250b0aae377729719b9ca838ef639a59a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hatlabs/signalk-alert-rules/git/commits/c1199a24e791b615d8fef2d4ad367a16ff7e3463","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/407010?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mairas","id":407010,"login":"mairas","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzAxMA==","organizatio