raph panel and scroll inside the card\n\nThe Apps row was a grid with `align-items: start`, so the inspector grew\nfreely with its content. An app declaring a couple of dozen singleton\npackages made the Shared table taller than the graph and pushed the\nper-app findings panel far down the page.\n\nDrop the `align-items` override and contain the inspector''s size instead:\nthe graph panel is the only intrinsic contributor to the row, the default\n`stretch` hands that height back to the inspector card, and the tab body\nbecomes the scroller. Below 900px the panels stack, each owns a row and\nhugs its content again (the override is declared after the base rule so\nthe cascade resolves in its favour).\n\nTests: browser coverage over a workspace with 24 shared declarations\n(equal card heights, the overflow scrolls inside the card and not the\npage, the stacked layout still hugs content) plus static guards for the\nCSS contract.\n\n* docs(odd): record the inspector-height review receipt for b8cd023","tree":{"sha":"ddc117c0c13d4e63d05e61e36e02d93bb5a0aabf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gedu/repack-atlas/git/trees/ddc117c0c13d4e63d05e61e36e02d93bb5a0aabf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gedu/repack-atlas/git/commits/83045ae001fe6330729ba00997c75148ff495ed7","verification":{"payload":"tree ddc117c0c13d4e63d05e61e36e02d93bb5a0aabf\nparent c85d1f15d1054d1a877b929feff39b9c10fd19f4\nauthor edug <gedu@users.noreply.github.com> 1791318223 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791318223 +0200\n\nfix(studio): cap the inspector to the graph panel and scroll inside the card (#76)\n\n* fix(studio): cap the inspector to the graph panel and scroll inside the card\n\nThe Apps row was a grid with `align-items: start`, so the inspector grew\nfreely with its content. An app declaring a couple of dozen singleton\npackages made the Shared table taller than the graph and pushed the\nper-app findings panel far down the page.\n\nDrop the `align-items` override and contain the inspector''s size instead:\nthe graph panel is the only intrinsic contributor to the row, the default\n`stretch` hands that height back to the inspector card, and the tab body\nbecomes the scroller. Below 900px the panels stack, each owns a row and\nhugs its content again (the override is declared after the base rule so\nthe cascade resolves in its favour).\n\nTests: browser coverage over a workspace with 24 shared declarations\n(equal card heights, the overflow scrolls inside the card and not the\npage, the stacked layout still hugs content) plus static guards for the\nCSS contract.\n\n* docs(odd): record the inspector-height review receipt for b8cd023","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxVjPCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA26oQABalGZBe8tgx5QtpSYvrVI1l\n6TJOocx9TZQ0J4q+1zt1+nlDxDT3i6JxDazRqgjTk5pkhvGbWJ5evdyNVSpuCltg\nbsmZwCPvkv1Gxr/aY8erp1QxVZVk4cQhZpllSJjW3EiteVeBA0XQOoOncC6Mjwda\noMI55Etlr9ybM8evUL9XeZxMirAmhiwq4hWkOnwghHL8h+BfkVF+N/L1TMeNr6qH\nt4HSH7PWPkuoz244jNdnqu3aJoNCIsHcYHGnBq2XqPMbDoANwdjfIunPKwl7343H\noCdSVkaxvOI2Ofq+5aKdjmfOytT/6HRgJbK7NCt/srigMMSk8Il8QEWu+GQVK9Un\nrooVzND4mmtAa7bdKIeGdoUMe7monVUEsD7OFZztBB2s7lpksZKhxKVTpD/7uzZF\nA8RBpBL6f8VDnWqI/FKEQq1YDMpXSLGwO7fLFRsQQ/Asi6PNlxdeci1qqCuxqmHm\nAAtC5TcO+kelqM6YVqE/OJwHLGbQxHYmYKnVlfCcr6/LPj7jvIAMWMK3RUtBadbK\nojoSpRwNcy6f8wfUbodTDxIVeh/im5tgDPA0oG86Uqf9HjyEh6z2AgFW73BVtPD6\nB31FjGpv8btarMHjL5ltmv06tWfP5MoFG2WIfIlG66p2XJ3hd6G5S1X0/6FgCrI/\nvybyo25qZLEiv8Reoa6R\n=vRr9\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T20:23:43Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864