.com/repos/gedu/repack-atlas/commits/c7ed8322906a2ce3757df5409b5daddd9f7da2da"}],"sha":"d147683ffdecf82ba6c795bc88d85a976a04b731","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gedu/repack-atlas/commits/d147683ffdecf82ba6c795bc88d85a976a04b731"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1676818?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gedu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gedu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gedu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gedu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gedu","id":1676818,"login":"gedu","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzY4MTg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gedu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gedu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gedu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gedu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gedu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gedu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gedu/repack-atlas/commits/c7ed8322906a2ce3757df5409b5daddd9f7da2da/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T13:10:14Z","email":"gedu@users.noreply.github.com","name":"edug"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T13:10:14Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(dev-tui): keep the wizard clean on resize and frame busy-port conflicts (#66)\n\n* fix(dev-tui): keep the last answer in the recap panel and clear resize ghosts\n\nclose() flushes the queued final state with a sync rerender before unmount, so the last answered question lands in the panel. A resize listener prepended before ink''s deletes the rows the terminal re-wrapped on a shrink, which ink''s own erase cannot see.\n\n* feat(dev): frame busy-port conflicts in a dim yellow panel on the human TTY path\n\n* fix(dev-tui): guard ci parity, stderr tty, NO_COLOR and reflow sizes\n\nLock the wizard''s ink CI mirror to ink''s own is-in-ci with a parity test, frame busy-port conflicts only when stderr is a TTY, follow no-color.org (empty NO_COLOR keeps color) across banner, wizard and panel, and return no escape sequence for unusable terminal sizes.\n\n* fix(dev-tui): compensate resize only on reflowing terminals and never over-delete\n\nGate the resize compensation on an allowlist of terminals known to re-wrap on shrink, ignore unusable column readings, and size the deletion from the smaller of the last two committed frames so an uncertain case leaves a ghost border instead of erasing terminal content. Lock the machine-path conflict output (bare lines, no panel, no ESC) with a spawned-CLI test.\n\n* fix(dev-tui): truncate recap lines so the panel never outgrows a small window\n\n* feat(dev-tui): fall back to the wordmark banner on narrow terminals\n\n* docs(odd): record the tiny-window scrollback limitation and close the feature","tree":{"sha":"f50e035d30cd7d31651bf640ef61d734fc6f23f8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gedu/repack-atlas/git/trees/f50e035d30cd7d31651bf640ef61d734fc6f23f8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gedu/repack-atlas/git/commits/c7ed8322906a2ce3757df5409b5daddd9f7da2da","verification":{"payload":"tree f50e035d30cd7d31651bf640ef61d734fc6f23f8\nparent 562fe3cc3c29537db797606a2eca81d1a003c06b\nauthor edug <gedu@users.noreply.github.com> 1791205814 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791205814 +0200\n\nfeat(dev-tui): keep the wizard clean on resize and frame busy-port conflicts (#66)\n\n* fix(dev-tui): keep the last answer in the recap panel and clear resize ghosts\n\nclose() flushes the queued final state with a sync rerender before unmount, so the last answered question lands in the panel. A resize listener prepended before ink''s deletes the rows the terminal re-wrapped on a shrink, which ink''s own erase cannot see.\n\n* feat(dev): frame busy-port conflicts in a dim yellow panel on the human TTY path\n\n* fix(dev-tui): guard ci parity, stderr tty, NO_COLOR and reflow sizes\n\nLock the wizard''s ink CI mirror to ink''s own is-in-ci with a parity test, frame busy-port conflicts only when stderr is a TTY, follow no-color.org (empty NO_COLOR keeps color) across banner, wizard and panel, and return no escape sequence for unusable terminal sizes.\n\n* fix(dev-tui): compensate resize only on reflowing terminals and never over-delete\n\nGate the resize compensation on an allowlist of terminals known to re-wrap on shrink, ignore unusable column readings, and size the deletion from the smaller of the last two committed frames so an uncertain case leaves a ghost border instead of erasing terminal content. Lock the machine-path conflict output (bare lines, no panel, no ESC) with a spawned-CLI test.\n\n* fix(dev-tui): truncate recap lines so the panel never outgrows a small window\n\n* feat(dev-tui): fall back to the wordmark banner on narrow terminals\n\n* docs(odd): record the tiny-window scrollback limitation and close the feature","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqw6G2CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAokwQAEYOb0ldVvaZ9FODApyQsfNZ\nyXvPOLXjgaJzAkD/ApC6vRNupTG+39ZDJvjsAM44HrIUYOKM1RvzKlHNy4iFjD97\nc7a//IL090KZeQaXhjNfY7NJqCNJM/c4LPnkqtKly+ogFQ7kNlHvbLl5XUvkeFHD\npypwK3mC4E1KkzhuLOsWtDALWy+GLpxLYT49Bb1dJjM1uwW4LczqXH1Bi+0sJHTT\n9wrDEFR62YyVxPMNwhDsLTd3GL2VOKe0heA/xtawXQG0S8AFjlU+t237hQIKoBVb\n+r26acufeev+ZtNWR6ZhoiTlz2Ap0MjptBp4CTG86HTA/cK8Mu7pVNiwS7nLI26B\nM4XaTt+pRHEFgLKRpplNDKkNjIR96cCAzSsCbzcM6XR114jnlskrWH4BEsZoQufz\nnRkaK//3GNGnU9ebrWvZaTVoDyH6qGNKvrJbT/laeShmk6njU/N6K5BeTtsGtiLW\nM3bd5L/CwkKn8h34Zra4xjMYYbb8oEpEHMDNbrYIZtAA6cMwAtK2ZY927KSQ1n22\nQR60g1YeIxh4DXOTgEYQEX4BG4cR9W9IwDwoP7P3TXOElifTmVlcNyBbWJwZd3AZ\n34ZSQLOKf4tZQaWPTYu8VSmonzHLLZj+Hi4BnqNhe+Zt5JtGwZM3W+jVy7dKYxXS\n4TZQyR49aP5ddtxTKDqL\n=tZUp\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-05T13:10:15Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/gedu/repack-atlas/commit/c7ed8322906a2ce3757df5409b5daddd9f7da2da","node_id":"C_kwDOUy7AttoAKGM3ZWQ4MzIyOTA2YTJjZTM3NTdkZjU0MDliNWRhZGRkOWY3ZGEyZGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/gedu/repack-atlas/commit/562fe3cc3c29537db797606a2eca81d1a003c06b","sha":"562fe3cc3c29537db797606a2eca81d1a003c06b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gedu/repack-atlas/commits/562fe3cc3c29537db797606a2eca81d1a003c06b"}],"sha":"c7ed8322906a2ce3757df5409b5daddd9f7da2da","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gedu/repack-atlas/commits/c7ed8322906a2ce3757df5409b5daddd9f7da2da"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1676818?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gedu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gedu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gedu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gedu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gedu","id":1676818,"login":"gedu","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzY4MTg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gedu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gedu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gedu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gedu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gedu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gedu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gedu/repack-atlas/commits/562fe3cc3c29537db797606a2eca81d1a003c06b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T09:09:43Z","email":"gedu@users.noreply.github.com","name":"edug"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T09:09:43Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(dev-tui): frame the wizard recap in a summary panel (#65)\n\n* fix(dev): elide busy-port owner commands from the middle\n\nWhat identifies an owning process is the tail of its argv (the app path and\n''cli.js start --port N''); the old end-elision threw exactly that away, so\nevery wizard ''(in use: ...)'' note showed only a truncated head. Over-cap\ncommands now shorten $HOME to ~ and drop a redundant leading ''node ''\nbefore eliding, and elide the middle on a path boundary so head and tail\nsurvive. The 100-char cap contract is unchanged; commands that already fit\nstay byte-identical.\n\nIssue #58 follow-up (D2).\n\n* feat(dev-tui): frame the wizard recap in a summary panel\n\nThe settled answers ran flush against the `dev:` error lines that follow a\nport conflict and read as plain scrollback. They now render inside one dim\nrounded panel (the dashboard''s border idiom) that hugs the widest recap\nline, with a blank line separating it from the live question and from\nwhatever the CLI prints after the wizard closes.\n\nThe panel replaces ink''s <Static>: a Static block prints one bare line per\nsettled question and cannot be framed as one summary. Measured on ink 6.8\nwith a fake non-TTY stdout, ink''s teardown leaves the final frame standing,\nso the panel survives close exactly as the Static output did. Assertions\nthat need a live frame write are gated on ink''s own is-in-ci predicate, as\nthe CI-mode fix in #63 established.\n\nIssue #58 follow-up (D2).\n\n* docs(odd): record wizard recap panel work units and evidence\n\n* fix(dev-tui): keep the recap panel separated after the wizard closes\n\nA real-PTY run (node dist/cli.js dev under a pty with live port owners)\nshowed the `dev:` conflict lines landing flush under the standing frame:\nthe panel''s blank row belonged to the live question, and when the wizard\ndied mid-flow there was no live question left to own it. The panel now\nalways renders its own trailing blank row, and the prompt port''s close()\nwrites one newline after unmount so whatever the caller prints next\nstarts below the final frame.\n\nNo machine path is affected: the TUI prompt port only exists for the\nhuman-interactive gate.","tree":{"sha":"c45272d7a84fdc9c34f52fffe3ccbf65554f93f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gedu/repack-atlas/git/trees/c45272d7a84fdc9c34f52fffe3ccbf65554f93f5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gedu/repack-atlas/git/commits/562fe3cc3c29537db797606a2eca81d1a003c06b","verification":{"payload":"tree c45272d7a84fdc9c34f52fffe3ccbf65554f93f5\nparent d7fe4bca6a4f6e8d29a155373ee1a444f3d4c480\nauthor edug <gedu@users.noreply.github.com> 1791191383 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791191383 +0200\n\nfeat(dev-tui): frame the wizard recap in a summary panel (#65)\n\n* fix(dev): elide busy-port owner commands from the middle\n\nWhat identifies an owning process is the tail of its argv (the app path and\n''cli.js start --port N''); the old end-elision threw exactly that away, so\nevery wizard ''(in use: ...)'' note showed only a truncated head. Over-cap\ncommands now shorten $HOME to ~ and drop a redundant leading ''node ''\nbefore eliding, and elide the middle on a path boundary so head and tail\nsurvive. The 100-char cap contract is unchanged; commands that already fit\nstay byte-identical.\n\nIssue #58 follow-up (D2).\n\n* feat(dev-tui): frame the wizard recap in a summary panel\n\nThe settled answers ran flush against the `dev:` error lines that follow a\nport conflict and read as plain scrollback. They now render inside one dim\nrounded panel (the dashboard''s border idiom) that hugs the widest recap\nline, with a blank line separating it from the live question and from\nwhatever the CLI prints after the wizard closes.\n\nThe panel replaces ink''s <Static>: a Static block prints one bare line per\nsettled question and cannot be framed as one summary. Measured on ink 6.8\nwith a fake non-TTY stdout, ink''s teardown leaves the final frame standing,\nso the panel survives close exactly as the Static output did. Assertions\nthat need a live frame write are gated on ink''s own is-in-ci predicate, as\nthe CI-mode fix in #63 established.\n\nIssue #58 follow-up (D2).\n\n* docs(odd): record wizard recap panel work units and evidence\n\n* fix(dev-tui): keep the recap panel separated after the wizard closes\n\nA real-PTY run (node dist/cli.js dev under a pty with live port owners)\nshowed the `dev:` conflict lines landing flush under the standing frame:\nthe panel''s blank row belonged to the live question, and when the wizard\ndied mid-flow there was no live question left to own it. The panel now\nalways renders its own trailing blank row, and the prompt port''s close()\nwrites one newline after unmount so whatever the caller prints next\nstarts below the final frame.\n\nNo machine path is affected: the TUI prompt port only exists for the\nhuman-interactive gate.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqw2lXCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA0y0QAE+3G7oPVfvl5TWYMN6EH33h\nZSYgZgmuSwH/WcpseAGbIm2FCPc9EzeIf4tZOLWpWMl9+BM3sG7IoDagxF/j59kz\nmfW4Ut0NrCb3CO9IxXMZ7HE5ypa9Dipp55xEPM/z1HBAvzyzIF3X67gqE3/JYI6x\nsdltAqK0fn4KKlyUUUAlDyDu1ciWUvsWbVqvwArJT