i.github.com/repos/gedu/repack-atlas/commits/68cc9d90cdfdf06f8db419e9e400b1eab637e4d7"}],"sha":"8f0c340bd9d011aa2cc1b0a0d6cc110fb8b15261","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gedu/repack-atlas/commits/8f0c340bd9d011aa2cc1b0a0d6cc110fb8b15261"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1676818?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gedu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gedu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gedu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gedu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gedu","id":1676818,"login":"gedu","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzY4MTg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gedu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gedu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gedu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gedu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gedu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gedu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gedu/repack-atlas/commits/68cc9d90cdfdf06f8db419e9e400b1eab637e4d7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T12:32:18Z","email":"gedu@users.noreply.github.com","name":"edug"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T12:32:18Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(dev): interactive TUI dashboard with wizard-in-TUI and startup banner (#59)\n\n* chore(dev): add ink for the interactive dev TUI\n\nAdds ink (v6) + react as runtime deps and @types/react as a dev\ndep, enables jsx (react-jsx) in the src and test tsconfigs, and\nrewrites AGENTS.md rule 11 to name them as exception (b): scoped to\nthe interactive dev TUI dashboard (src/cli/dev-tui/**), lazy-loaded\nvia dynamic import so --json, --ci and non-TTY paths never import\nthem. Also notes dev-tui/ in the layout.\n\n* feat(dev): add pure TUI view-model with spinner collapsing\n\n* feat(dev): render dev dashboard TUI with sidebar and log panel\n\n* feat(dev): mount the TUI for interactive dev sessions\n\nThe ink dashboard renders only for a human at a TTY: no --json, no\n--ci, TTY stdin and stdout. ink, react and the dev-tui render layer\nare dynamic-imported inside that gate, so machine paths (--json,\n--ci, non-TTY, --dry-run) never load them (AGENTS.md rule 11\nexception (b)); tests/cli/dev-tui-seam.test.ts locks this by static\nanalysis since eslint has no ink/react rule. Plain output stays\nbyte-identical, and a TUI mount failure degrades to plain rendering\nwith a warning instead of failing the session.\n\n* docs(odd): track dev TUI dashboard task document\n\nFeature doc with scope, constraints and per-task evidence for the interactive dev dashboard (ink TUI).\n\n* docs(odd): record dev TUI closure evidence and review defect\n\nParent spot check 618/618; native review START blocked by upstream defect (GentleAI/gentle-ai#4749 occurrence filed).\n\n* fix(dev): TUI wheel routing, copy gutter, live spinners, pinned progress, Re.Pack palette\n\nFollow-up polish from the first real-terminal smoke (odd doc F1-F5): mouse-tracking routes the wheel by column (panel scrolls, sidebar selects) with shift+drag copy noted; the sidebar border replaces the text gutter so log selection copies clean; collapsed spinner dots animate on the 100ms tick; the active progress bar pins to the panel bottom and un-pins once history flows past it; colors follow Re.Pack''s reporter (colored level symbol, plain message).\n\n* fix(dev): TUI scroll clamp, dot collapse, bar completion, ascii glyphs, activity, mouse toggle\n\nF6  logWindow clamps the offset to max(0, total - pageHeight), so\n    scrolling past the top shows the first page instead of a blank\n    panel; key/wheel scroll handlers clamp against the same max.\nF7  the collapse normalizer drops the <=6 trailing-dots cap: a dots\n    flood of any length (Building........) collapses to one frame.\nF8  a terminal build line (success kind, error kind, or\n    /compiled|success/i) after the newest progress bar kills the pin\n    immediately and settles the bar as ONE completed 100% frame at\n    its place in the body flow (completeProgressFrame +\n    isTerminalBuildLine, pure and tested). Recency un-pin unchanged.\nF9  leading-symbol detection accepts Re.Pack''s ascii fallback set\n    (i ! x ✓ ->) when space-separated, colored per the F5 map;\n    splitTimestamp dims the leading [hh:mm:ss.SSSZ] span only.\nF10 the model counts log lines arriving while a row is not selected\n    (markViewed clears); the sidebar renders a subtle bouncing badge\n    (glyph + count, capped 99+) that never shows on the watched row.\nF11 m toggles mouse reporting: OFF writes the DECSET-off sequence,\n    wheel routing is state-gated (stale SGR bytes are inert), native\n    drag-copy works without Shift; the footer reflects the state.\n\nVerified: pnpm build/typecheck/lint exit 0; pnpm test 655/655\n(was 638; +17 pure/app tests).\n\n* feat(dev): type lines into the selected app stdin from the TUI\n\nF12 typed input, end to end:\n- core/ports: ProcessHandle gains the OPTIONAL writeStdin(data):\n  boolean (existing fakes/stubs keep compiling; false = nothing\n  writable received it).\n- adapters/process-runner: children spawn with stdin PIPED (was\n  ignored); the real handle writes child.stdin when writable and an\n  EPIPE after death reports false instead of crashing the host.\n- runner/supervisor: writeAppInput(key|name, line) routes line+\\n to\n  the live child of one supervised app (same key-or-name resolver as\n  the statuses); false with no live child, no writeStdin, or during\n  shutdown. One-shot children stay non-routable (transient).\n- cli/dev seam: onSendInput callback into the TUI wired to\n  supervisor.writeAppInput.\n- TUI: i opens a one-line prompt (›) at the panel bottom when the\n  selected row is a supervised app; printable appends, Backspace\n  trims, Esc cancels, Enter sends the exact line and closes; the mode\n  swallows the whole keymap, and the footer says exactly\n  ''i send line to stdin'' — nothing more.\n\nCAVEAT (stated in the code, not promised in the UI): children spawn\nwith piped stdin, so the bytes DO reach the child process, but the\nreact-native CLI reads interactive shortcuts (r reload etc.) only\nfrom a TTY stdin — piped lines reach the bundler process, effects\ndepend on the child actually reading stdin (esbuild/rspack watchers\nwon''t react; rs-style RN keypresses may be ignored).\n\nVerified: pnpm build/typecheck/lint exit 0; pnpm test 663/663.\n\n* docs(odd): record F6-F12 closure and evidence\n\nUnits f2d8a1d + ecf01c5; parent spot check 663/663.\n\n* docs(odd): rules audit and G1-G5 work items\n\n* fix(dev): scroll-pause new-lines notice and numberless activity badge\n\n* fix(dev): restore the terminal when a mounted TUI crashes\n\n* feat(dev): print a startup banner with an atlas glyph on human runs\n\n* docs(odd): record G1-G4 closure and evidence\n\n* feat(dev): redraw the startup banner with the balloon artwork\n\nReplace the hand-drawn globe with the user-supplied braille hot-air\nballoon carrying the REPACK lettering, reproduced verbatim (24 rows,\n38 cols). Top crown and basket/rope rows in Re.Pack green, balloon\nbody in pink 38;5;213; charset stays Ghostty-safe, centering and the\ncolor/no-color split unchanged. The row-budget test now locks the\n24+2-row layout.\n\n* feat(dev): render the dev wizard prompts in the TUI visual language\n\n* test(dev): cover the TUI wizard prompt port\n\nThe ink wizard shipped with no tests. This adds the coverage the design\ndepends on, in the three layers the implementation is split into:\n\n- dev-tui-wizard.test.ts: the pure machine (openField per kind, clamped\n  cursor, option-order toggles, validate-stays-open submit, sticky\n  cancel) plus the purity fence dev-tui-seam.test.ts runs on model.ts.\n- dev-tui-wizard-app.test.tsx: WizardApp render/repaint through\n  ink-testing-library, including real keystrokes via useInput.\n- dev-tui-wizard-port.test.ts: createTuiPromptPort terminal hygiene on\n  fake streams - raw mode taken and handed back, cursor shown, stdin\n  paused, dangling question cancelled, close idempotent.\n- dev-tui-seam.test.ts: the ink port is now inside the rule-11 static\n  fence, and the G5 routing is proven both ways (TUI condition live ->\n  ink port; non-TTY stdin -> env.createPrompts; machine flags -> none).\n\nNo implementation change: the machine, view, and port behaved as designed.\n\n* docs(odd): record banner redraw and G5 wizard-in-TUI closure\n\n* docs(odd): record native review approval for the banner+G5 slice\n\n* fix(dev): resume stdin before mounting the dashboard TUI\n\nThe wizard''s close() and the mount gate leave process.stdin paused, and\nink 6 refs the stream without ever resuming it — a paused stream never\nfires ''readable'', so the dashboard''s useInput pipeline sat completely\ndeaf after the handoff: arrows, j/k and even q/Ctrl-C reached stdin but\nzero events ever reached the keymap (verified over a real pty: 5/5 ink\ninput events during the wizard, 0 after the alt-screen takeover).\nmountDevTui now resumes stdin right before render() and the finally\nparks it again, so a resumed TTY handle cannot keep the session alive.\n\n* feat(dev): select the app under a sidebar click in the TUI\n\nF13: a button-0 SGR press over a sidebar row selects that app directly\n(row r maps to roster index r-1; the sidebar list renders from screen\nrow 1), so the mouse the wheel already uses becomes a pointer. Clicks\nover the panel or below the roster stay swallowed mouse traffic, drag\nmotion (button 32) and modified clicks are deliberately not clicks, and\nthe whole route is gated on the F11 mouse-tracking toggle so stale bytes\nwith tracking off move nothing. The footer now says what the mouse does\nwhile it is on.\n\n* fix(dev): harden the TUI wizard against a caller bug and a bad teardown\n\nReview suggestions from the G5 slice:\n- wizard-model ask() answers a second concurrent call as cancelled\n  instead of orphaning the first (live) question''s promise forever;\n  the port is sequential-by-construction today, so this only turns a\n  future caller bug from a hang into an immediate cancelled answer.\n- the prompt port''s close() try/catches ink''s unmount, because the\n  cursor-restore / raw-mode-off / stdin-pause cleanup after it is what\n  the dashboard''s takeover relies on — a throwing teardown must not\n  skip it.","tree":{"sha":"cecab4805a5825f489820616914cf052e70c7d77","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gedu/repack-atlas/git/trees/cecab4805a5825f489820616914cf052e70c7d77"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gedu/repack-atlas/git/commits/68cc9d90cdfdf06f8db419e9e400b1eab637e4d7","verification":{"payload":"tree cecab4805a5825f489820616914cf052e70c7d77\nparent 791ec00cb0e883e9cf0af03df066c985d7aa6b47\nauthor edug <gedu@users.noreply.github.com> 1790944338 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790944338 +0200\n\nfeat(dev): interactive TUI dashboard with wizard-in-TUI and startup banner (#59)\n\n* chore(dev): add ink for the interactive dev TUI\n\nAdds ink (v6) + react as runtime deps and @types/react as a dev\ndep, enables jsx (react-jsx) in the src and test tsconfigs, and\nrewrites AGENTS.md rule 11 to name them as exception (b): scoped to\nthe interactive dev TUI dashboard (src/cli/dev-tui/**), lazy-loaded\nvia dynamic import so --json, --ci and non-TTY paths never import\nthem. Also notes dev-tui/ in the layout.\n\n* feat(dev): add pure TUI view-model with spinner collapsing\n\n* feat(dev): render dev dashboard TUI with sidebar and log panel\n\n* feat(dev): mount the TUI for interactive dev sessions\n\nThe ink dashboard renders only for a human at a TTY: no --json, no\n--ci, TTY stdin and stdout. ink, react and the dev-tui render layer\nare dynamic-imported inside that gate, so machine paths (--json,\n--ci, non-TTY, --dry-run) never load them (AGENTS.md rule 11\nexception (b)); tests/cli/dev-tui-seam.test.ts locks this by static\nanalysis since eslint has no ink/react rule. Plain output stays\nbyte-identical, and a TUI mount failure degrades to plain rendering\nwith a warning instead of failing the session.\n\n* docs(odd): track dev TUI dashboard task document\n\nFeature doc with scope, constraints and per-task evidence for the interactive dev dashboard (ink TUI).\n\n* docs(odd): record dev TUI closure evidence and review defect\n\nParent spot check 618/618; native review START blocked by upstream defect (GentleAI/gentle-ai#4749 occurrence filed).\n\n* fix(dev): TUI wheel routing, copy gutter, live spinners, pinned progress, Re.Pack palette\n\nFollow-up polish from the first real-terminal smoke (odd doc F1-F5): mouse-tracking routes the wheel by column (panel scrolls, sidebar selects) with shift+drag copy noted; the sidebar border replaces the text gutter so log selection copies clean; collapsed spinner dots animate on the 100ms tick; the active progress bar pins to the panel bottom and un-pins once history flows past it; colors follow Re.Pack''s reporter (colored level symbol, plain message).\n\n* fix(dev): TUI scroll clamp, dot collapse, bar completion, ascii glyphs, activity, mouse toggle\n\nF6  logWindow clamps the offset to max(0, total - pageHeight), so\n    scrolling past the top shows the first page instead of a blank\n    panel; key/wheel scroll handlers clamp against the same max.\nF7  the collapse normalizer drops the <=6 trailing-dots cap: a dots\n    flood of any length (Building........) collapses to one frame.\nF8  a terminal build line (success kind, error kind, or\n    /compiled|success/i) after the newest progress bar kills the pin\n    immediately and settles the bar as ONE completed 100% frame at\n    its place in the body flow (completeProgressFrame +\n    isTerminalBuildLine, pure and tested). Recency un-pin unchanged.\nF9  leading-symbol detection accepts Re.Pack''s ascii fallback set\n    (i ! x ✓ ->) when space-separated, colored per the F5 map;\n    splitTimestamp dims the leading [hh:mm:ss.SSSZ] span only.\nF10 the model counts log lines arriving while a row is not selected\n    (markViewed clears); the sidebar renders a subtle bouncing badge\n    (glyph + count, capped 99+) that never shows on the watched row.\nF11 m toggles mouse reporting: OFF writes the DECSET-off sequence,\n    wheel routing is state-gated (stale SGR bytes are inert), native\n    drag-copy works without Shift; the footer reflects the state.\n\nVerified: pnpm build/typecheck/lint exit 0; pnpm test 655/655\n(was 638; +17 pure/app tests).\n\n* feat(dev): type lines into the selected app stdin from the TUI\n\nF12 typed input, end to end:\n- core/ports: ProcessHandle gains the OPTIONAL writeStdin(data):\n  boolean (existing fakes/stubs keep compiling; false = nothing\n  writable received it).\n- adapters/process-runner: children spawn with stdin PIPED (was\n  ignored); the real handle writes child.stdin when writable and an\n  EPIPE after death reports false instead of crashing the host.\n- runner/supervisor: writeAppInput(key|name, line) routes line+\\n to\n  the live child of one supervised app (same key-or-name resolver as\n  the statuses); false with no live child, no writeStdin, or during\n  shutdown. One-shot children stay non-routable (transient).\n- cli/dev seam: onSendInput callback into the TUI wired to\n  supervisor.writeAppInput.\n- TUI: i opens a one-line prompt (›) at the panel bottom when the\n  selected row is a supervised app; printable appends, Backspace\n  trims, Esc cancels, Enter sends the exact line and closes; the mode\n  swallows the whole keymap, and the footer says exactly\n  ''i send line to stdin'' — nothing more.\n\nCAVEAT (stated in the code, not promised in the UI): children spawn\nwith piped stdin, so the bytes DO reach the child process, but the\nreact-native CLI reads interactive shortcuts (r reload etc.) only\nfrom a TTY stdin — piped lines reach the bundler process, effects\ndepend on the child actually reading stdin (esbuild/rspack watchers\nwon''t react; rs-style RN keypresses may be ignored).\n\nVerified: pnpm build/typecheck/lint exit 0; pnpm test 663/663.\n\n* docs(odd): record F6-F12 closure and evidence\n\nUnits f2d8a1d + ecf01c5; parent spot check 663/663.\n\n* docs(odd): rules audit and G1-G5 work items\n\n* fix(dev): scroll-pause new-lines notice and numberless activity badge\n\n* fix(dev): restore the terminal when a mounted TUI crashes\n\n* feat(dev): print a startup banner with an atlas glyph on human runs\n\n* docs(odd): record G1-G4 closure and evidence\n\n* feat(dev): redraw the startup banner with the balloon artwork\n\nReplace the hand-drawn globe with the user-supplied braille hot-air\nballoon carrying the REPACK lettering, reproduced verbatim (24 rows,\n38 cols). Top crown and basket/rope rows in Re.Pack green, balloon\nbody in pink 38;5;213; charset stays Ghostty-safe, centering and the\ncolor/no-color split unchanged. The row-budget test now locks the\n24+2-row layout.\n\n* feat(dev): render the dev wizard prompts in the TUI visual language\n\n* test(dev): cover the TUI wizard prompt port\n\nThe ink wizard shipped with no tests. This adds the coverage the design\ndepends on, in the three layers the implementation is split into:\n\n- dev-tui-wizard.test.ts: the pure machine (openField per kind, clamped\n  cursor, option-order toggles, validate-stays-open submit, sticky\n  cancel) plus the purity fence dev-tui-seam.test.ts runs on model.ts.\n- dev-tui-wizard-app.test.tsx: WizardApp render/repaint through\n  ink-testing-library, including real keystrokes via useInput.\n- dev-tui-wizard-port.test.ts: createTuiPromptPort terminal hygiene on\n  fake streams - raw mode taken and handed back, cursor shown, stdin\n  paused, dangling question cancelled, close idempotent.\n- dev-tui-seam.test.ts: the ink port is now inside the rule-11 static\n  fence, and the G5 routing is proven both ways (TUI condition live ->\n  ink port; non-TTY stdin -> env.createPrompts; machine flags -> none).\n\nNo implementation change: the machine, view, and port behaved as designed.\n\n* docs(odd): record banner redraw and G5 wizard-in-TUI closure\n\n* docs(odd): record native review approval for the banner+G5 slice\n\n* fix(dev): resume stdin before mounting the dashboard TUI\n\nThe wizard''s close() and the mount gate leave process.stdin paused, and\nink 6 refs the stream without ever resuming it — a paused stream never\nfires ''readable'', so the dashboard''s useInput pipeline sat completely\ndeaf after the handoff: arrows, j/k and even q/Ctrl-C reached stdin but\nzero events ever reached the keymap (verified over a real pty: 5/5 ink\ninput events during the wizard, 0 after the alt-screen takeover).\nmountDevTui now resumes stdin right before render() and the finally\nparks it again, so a resumed TTY handle cannot keep the session alive.\n\n* feat(dev): select the app under a sidebar click in the TUI\n\nF13: a button-0 SGR press over a sidebar row selects that app directly\n(row r maps to roster index r-1; the sidebar list renders from screen\nrow 1), so the mouse the wheel already uses becomes a pointer. Clicks\nover the panel or below the roster stay swallowed mouse traffic, drag\nmotion (button 32) and modified clicks are deliberately not clicks, and\nthe whole route is gated on the F11 mouse-tracking toggle so stale bytes\nwith tracking off move nothing. The footer now says what the mouse does\nwhile it is on.\n\n* fix(dev): harden the TUI wizard against a caller bug and a bad teardown\n\nReview suggestions from the G5 slice:\n- wizard-model ask() answers a second concurrent call as cancelled\n  instead of orphaning the first (live) question''s promise forever;\n  the port is sequential-by-construction today, so this only turns a\n  future caller bug from a hang into an immediate cancelled answer.\n- the prompt port''s close() try/catches ink''s unmount, because the\n  cursor-restore / raw-mode-off / stdin-pause cleanup after it is what\n  the dashboard''s takeover relies on — a throwing teardown must not\n  skip it.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqv6RSCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAIV0QAJrbQdjPeexq23aRHtzNQcWA\nCEwhkGq9wYAc0TC++zg9gTR4JnoNFf0s5qbhJ2+CWFQJ7WxVm69SpWtKOR3H9mWb\nP3oK4XekHfJKJGM1IxmKD2AF0HTsl2E/hJHKt1ja26Kq8SkFDzmI6AgqbumS7JqB\nIgTL2GGkxWNg8CtofyUPT52w/xJFYYS1NahL7kMEpxOVQGcY2MuKM37X6Z1j8CV+\nxCqed+nIsoD2HTDTllA9B8oUHlnAVnGYG2bgfj9ySqoe0S3Tl1swaIP4p8FGF8Mo\n3iDk+ITpFzlqPj2PX2RNVuF+bCWc0iEFenSRmnJeriDt9NT8Sp2t2qydbVaaeBzg\n/80CkVIuNoikVMdVhipXpb2lQ0g+SrdxDWmDARe7x3uPjjObqd7gRYXhEnUgET/W\nVmwRGhQJC1ZVqSQfy05vK+P9ioxueUU2Z9zBfNofQihs7bfjMJoVdbkA9VhWG1AY\nKRLJYGG455jccTbJRkbbJFFCNaZGZcxocbu6JmSXwmwPKYQerjXWUL5QuwhSZNrq\nxotw9Fo516MssO4CdKiKZojtZUFcEn+lpq48uZdZ/oOoiqME+hnLTe6xbzQpnHah\nrpHX0y3/LzY6oph86vRH2KEKR2AWH9Vcvp+yOmLUOtbosnZxX5VaXM7fqxEvFNEc\nyUTtkQ7WTkOEHvbhTU8s\n=j08/\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-02T12:32:19Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url